hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9001","Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih. 8997 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi and Abu Dawud narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"9002","8998 - And Hilal ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it, and he added, he said: And the dream of the believer is a part of forty-five parts of prophethood."
"9003","8999 - Hilal ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me."
"9004","9000 - And Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Advise me. He said: Do not become angry. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this angle, except for an angle concerning which there is disagreement."
"9005","9001 - Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was sent while I and the Hour are like these two, and he pointed with the index finger and the one next to it."
"9006","9002 - Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id, Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim, and Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, they said: Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Sharik and Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Render the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain."
"9007","9003 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Amr ibn Khuza'ah ibn Luhayy ibn Qama'ah ibn Jundub. (i.e. the one who changed the religion; the matn here is abbreviated.)"
"9008","9004 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no 'adwa (contagion conveying illness by itself), no tiyarah (evil omen), and no Safar (omen in the month of Safar)."
"9009","9005 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the day of fasting of one of you, let him not utter foul speech nor act corruptly; and if someone acts ignorantly toward him, let him say: I am a fasting person."
"9010","9006 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah cursed the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their prices. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this angle with this chain."
"9011","9007 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his 'asabah (male relatives); and whoever leaves a burden - I think he said: - then it is upon him (i.e. the responsibility falls on the speaker)."
"9012","9008 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wisal (continuous fasting without breaking), so they said: You practice wisal. He said: I am not like you; I spend the night with my Lord, He feeds me and gives me drink."
"9013","9009 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn Yusuf al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wretched is the slave of the dinar, the dirham, the qatifah (velvet cloak) and the khamisah (striped garment); if he is given he is pleased, and if he is not given he is not pleased."
"9014","9010 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Qur'an used to be reviewed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every year; then in the year in which he passed away it was reviewed with him twice, and he used to observe i'tikaf in the last ten of Ramadan, then in the year in which he passed away he observed i'tikaf for twenty days. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this angle."
"9015","9011 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Richness is not from abundance of goods, but richness is richness of the soul."
"9016","9012 - Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says on the Day of Resurrection: I am the best of partners; so whoever associatetd a partner with Me, then all of it is for him."
"9017","9013 - Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People are mines like the mines of gold and silver; so the best of them in Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they attain understanding."
"9018","9014 - Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, raising it (marfu'), he said: A man wearing two cloaks passed by, swaggering in them, so he was swallowed by the earth; and he keeps sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"9019","9015 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said - I think he said: - The Hour will not come - or: the days will not pass - until a man rules who will conquer Constantinople and the mountain of al-Daylam."
"9020","9016 - 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of this world will not pass until a man from me (my household) rules, and even if only one day remained of this world, Allah would lengthen that day until he conquers Constantinople and al-Daylam."
"9021","9017 - Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn and 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The mine is jubar (no liability), and the well is jubar, and in rikaz (buried treasure) is the fifth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Husayn nor from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, except Qays."
"9022","9018 - Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh: the most affectionate to a child, and the most careful with a husband regarding what is in his hand."
"9023","Qudamah ibn Musa. 9019 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti and Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisisi narrated to us, they said: Abu Qatan 'Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, from Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Salamah, from Qudamah ibn Musa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, set right for me my religion which is the safeguard of my affair, and set right for me my world in which is my livelihood, and set right for me my Hereafter to which is my return, and make life an increase for me in every good, and make death a relief for me from every evil. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle."
"9024","'Asim ibn Bahdalah. 9020 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is what you give out of self-sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. Your wife says: Feed me or divorce me; and your child says: To whom do you entrust us? And your servant says: Spend on me - I think he said: - or sell me."
"9025","9021 - And Ahmad ibn al-Hakam ibn Zibyan narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought as if it is a wide-eyed ram, and it will be stopped between Paradise and Hell, then it will be said: O people of Paradise; so they will crane their necks and look. And it will be said: O people of Hell; so they will crane their necks and look. Then it will be slaughtered, and it will be said: Eternity, no death."
"9026","9022 - And with it (the same chain) he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Fire complained to its Lord, saying: Parts of me have consumed others; so He made for it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer. So severe heat is from its hot wind, and severe cold is from its zamharir (intense cold). And this hadith from 'Asim, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9027","9023 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the 'Isha prayer one night until it was a third of the night; then he came while there was languor among the people, and they were in scattered groups and circles, so he became angry and said: If a man called people to a bone with meat or two arrow-heads (marmatayn), they would respond, yet they stay behind from this prayer. I had resolved to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then command those who stay behind from this prayer that it be set ablaze upon them with fires. And this hadith was narrated by 'Asim, and Hammad and Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated it from him, and Hammad has the better rendering of it."
"9028","9024 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, raises a man a degree, so he says: How is this for me? So He says: By the supplication of your child for you. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hammad from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah."
"9029","9025 - And with it he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or keep silent."
"9030","9026 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9031","9027 - Ahmad ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, 'Arim and Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer at the moment he fornicates, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer at the moment he steals, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer at the moment he drinks it; faith is stripped from his heart, then if he repents, Allah turns to him."
"9032","9028 - And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu 'Ali al-Hanafi 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The qintar is twelve thousand uqiyyah, each uqiyyah greater than what is between heaven and earth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurairah, and we do not know for it any path except this path; and others than al-Hanafi reported it with a connected chain, while a group reported it as mawquf (stopped)."
"9033","9029 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has one hundred mercies; with Him are ninety-nine, and He placed among you one mercy by which you show mercy to one another; then when the Day of Resurrection comes, He will join it to them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it with a chain from Hammad except Abd al-Samad."
"9034","9030 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Isa son of Maryam will descend as a just judge and a just imam; he will break the cross, kill the pig and the monkeys, and prostration will be one, for Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"9035","9031 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; then when they say it, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"9036","9032 - And with it (the same chain) he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aim for moderation and correctness (qaribu wa saddidu)."
"9037","9033 - And with it he said, he said: Severe heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool (the prayer) by praying Zuhr in severe heat. And these hadiths were narrated by Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, known through him."
"9038","9034 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, a man finds in himself what he would not like to speak of, though he had all that is in this world? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is pure faith."
"9039","9035 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qur'an will come on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Lord, adorn him! - meaning the one who recited it - so he will be dressed with the crown of honor, or the robe of honor; then it will say: O Lord, increase him, so he will be dressed with the robe of honor; then it will say: O Lord, increase him, so he will be adorned with the robe of honor; then it will say: O Lord, be pleased with him, so He will be pleased with him."
"9040","9036 - And Bishr ibn Adam narrated it to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abd al-Samad, from Shu'bah."
"9041","9037 - Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the last 'Isha one night until a third of the night had passed or nearly; then he came out to us while the people were in scattered groups, and he became severely angry, then said: If a man called people to a fat bone and two arrow-heads, they would respond while they hear; I had resolved to command men to carry bundles of firewood, then stay behind to people whose folks do not attend the prayer, and set it ablaze upon them with fire. Then Ibn Umm Maktum the blind came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a blind man whose house is far, and I have no guide who suits me; do you find for me any concession? He said: Does the call reach you? He said: Yes. He said: I find no concession for you. And this hadith, part of its wording was narrated by Hammad and Abu Bakr, and part of it we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, except Zayd - the story of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"9042","9038 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah - I think he raised it (marfu') - he said: A woman was punished for a cat which she tied up; she neither fed it nor gave it drink, nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, except Isra'il."
"9043","9039 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It would not please me to have Uhud as gold and die on the day I die with a dirham of it with me, except a dirham I set aside for a creditor."
"9044","9040 - Abu Kurayb and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There was between Khalid ibn al-Walid and Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf some of what occurs between people, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave my Companions for me; for if one of you spent the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of them, nor half of it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, except Za'idah, nor from Za'idah except Husayn ibn 'Ali."
"9045","9041 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is killed by plague is a martyr, and whoever is killed by his belly (disease) is a martyr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, except 'Imran."
"9046","9042 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Bakka'i narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from 'Asim and Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The mine is jubar, the well is jubar, and in rikaz is the fifth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim and Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, except Qays."
"9047","9043 - Al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Fire was stoked for a thousand years until it turned red, then stoked for a thousand years until it turned white, and a thousand years until it turned black; so it is black and dark. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it with a chain except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, from Sharik."
"9048","9044 - And Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw as if I was at a well drawing water, then Abu Bakr came and drew a bucket or two, and in his drawing was weakness, and Allah forgives him; then 'Umar came and it turned into a large water-skin (bag), and I never saw a genius among people working as he worked. This or something like it, or as he said: I doubt the wording of Abu Bakr."
"9049","9045 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves wealth - I think he said: - and does not pay its due, it will be made on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent with two spots, and it will follow him until it puts its hand (mouth) in his mouth, and it will keep biting it until judgment is finished among the servants - meaning until the reckoning among the servants is finished."
"9050","9046 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the belly of one of you to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, except Abu Ja'far al-Razi."
"9051","9047 - And Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Ibrahim was cast into the Fire, he said: O Allah, You are One in heaven, and I am one on earth worshipping You. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Asim except Abu Ja'far, nor from Abu Ja'far except Ishaq, and we heard it only from Abu Hisham."
"9052","9048 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ruwaym al-Muqri narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was aided with terror (cast into enemies), and 'Ad were destroyed by al-dabur (the west wind). And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this angle with this chain, and Ruwaym alone narrated it from Sallam."
"9053","9049 - Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding (They will remain therein for ages): He said: The hiqb (age) is eighty years. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who raised it (marfu') except al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr, from Hammam; others report it as mawquf."
"9054","9050 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor a livestock dog, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"9055","9051 - And al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated it to us, Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, raising it (marfu') with the like of it. And we do not know anyone who reported this hadith with a chain except Yazid, from Hammad ibn Zayd, and Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah, and others besides them only with his chain."
"9056","Suhayl, from his father. 9052 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers; for he does not know in which of them is the blessing."
"9057","9053 - And Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not initiate the Jews and Christians with salam; and when you meet them on the roads, force them to its narrowest part."
"9058","9054 - And Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; Allah will grant victory at his hands. 'Umar said: I never loved leadership except that day. So he called 'Ali and sent him, saying: Go and fight until Allah grants victory at your hands, and do not turn around. So he walked a while, then stopped and did not turn around, saying: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall I fight them? He said: Fight them until they say: There is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; then when they do that, they protect from you their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"9059","9055 - Hamdan ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pen is lifted from three: from the child until he grows up, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the insane until he recovers."
"9060","9056 - Ishaq narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Al-'Abbas branded a camel of his on its face, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why not on a bone other than the face? He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall brand only on the last bone of it; so he branded on the buttocks."
"9061","9057 - And with it (the same chain) he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us with tying the mouths of water-skins and overturning vessels."
"9062","9058 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us, when one of us took his bed, to say: O Allah, You are the Lord of the heavens, Lord of the earth, and Lord of everything; Splitter of the grain and the seed, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel and the Qur'an; I seek refuge in You from the evil of every possessor of evil whose forelock You hold; You are the First, there is nothing before You; the Last, there is nothing after You; the Manifest, there is nothing above You; the Hidden, there is nothing beneath You; settle my debt for me, and free me from poverty. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9063","9059 - Taliq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Do you not see the moon on the night of full moon without difficulty in seeing it? We said: Yes indeed. He said: By Allah, you shall see Him just as you see the moon on the night of full moon. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn 'Uyaynah more completely than this wording, and Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated it; both narrated it from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9064","9060 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir - meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid - narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that Fatimah, may Allah's mercy be upon her, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for a servant, so he said: Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than that? Glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times. And this hadith was narrated by Suhayl from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him; and al-A'mash narrated from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, something similar with other than its wording."
"9065","9061 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man rises from his seat then returns to it, he has more right to it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, except Suhayl."
"9066","9062 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to sit upon a live coal until his clothes burn is better for him than to sit upon a grave. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, except from the hadith of Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9067","9063 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves a servant, He calls Jibril, peace be upon him: I have loved so-and-so, so love him; so Jibril calls out in heaven, then love for him is sent down among the people of earth; and that is His saying: (Those who believe and do righteous deeds, the Most Merciful will appoint for them affection). And when He hates a servant, He calls Jibril: I have hated so-and-so. So he calls out among the people of heaven, then hatred is sent down among the people of earth. And this hadith was narrated by Suhayl, al-A'mash, and Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9068","9064 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should leave (prayer) until he hears a sound or finds wind. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from the hadith of Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9069","9065 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quti'i narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him. (The matn is suspended here; its completion is in the next narration.)"
"9070","9066 - And Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that a man came and said: I did not sleep last night. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: From what? He said: A scorpion stung me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you said in the evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, nothing would have harmed you. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah; and more than one narrated it from Suhayl, from his father, from a man among the companions of his father. And Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it from Suhayl, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abis."
"9071","9067 - And with the chain of Ahmad ibn Aban he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent man is Abu Bakr; what an excellent man is 'Umar ibn al-Khattab; what an excellent man is Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah; what an excellent man is Mu'adh ibn 'Amr ibn al-Jamuh; what an excellent man is Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, except Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad."
"9072","9068 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Souls are marshalled troops; those of them that recognize one another unite, and those that are unacquainted differ. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from the hadith of Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9073","9069 - And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu from (eating) a piece of dried cheese (thawr aqit), then he was seen eating a sheep's shoulder, then he prayed and did not perform wudu."
"9074","9070 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Hira with Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, Talhah and al-Zubayr, when the rock shook; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be still; for upon you is only a Prophet, or a Siddiq, or a martyr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, except Abd al-'Aziz."
"9075","9071 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until wealth increases and overflows, until a man goes out with the zakat of his wealth and finds no one to accept it from him, and until al-harj increases. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-harj? He said: Killing. And until the land of the Arabs returns to meadows and rivers. And this hadith, part of it has been narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from other angles; and we do not know anyone who took it except Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9076","9072 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Uthman - meaning al-Ghatafani - narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"9077","9073 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not travel more than three (days) except with a mahram. Thus Suhayl said, from his father, from Abu Hurairah; and al-A'mash narrated it from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id."
"9078","9074 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) congratulated a man on marriage (raffa'a), he said: May Allah bless for you, bless upon you, and join between you upon good. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, except Abd al-'Aziz."
"9079","9075 - And with it, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him: that some women of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot come to you with the men; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your appointment is the house of so-and-so woman. So he came, spoke with them, then said: No three children of one of you die and she seeks reward for them except she enters Paradise. A woman among them said: Or two? He said: And two."
"9080","9076 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who does not pay the zakat of his wealth except he and his wealth will be brought, and plates in the Fire of Hell will be heated for him, and his forehead, brow and back will be branded with them, until Allah, Exalted, judges between His servants on a day whose measure is a thousand years of what you count; then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to Hell. And no servant who does not pay the sadaqah of his camels except he and his camels will be brought in their fullest state, and a wide flat plain will be spread for them, and they will walk over him; every time the last of them passes, the first of them is returned, until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, judges between His servants; then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to Hell. And no servant who does not pay the sadaqah of his sheep except he and his sheep will be brought in their fullest state, and a wide flat plain will be spread for them, and they will walk over him; every time the last of them passes from him, the first is returned upon him; they will tread him with their hooves and gore him with their horns; among them is neither one with twisted horns nor one without horns, until Allah judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years; then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to Hell. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and horses? He said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. And horses are for three: for a man a reward, for a man a cover, and upon a man a burden. As for the one for whom it is a reward: the one who keeps it in the path of Allah and prepares it for Him; it is a reward for him - nothing disappears in their bellies except reward is written for him for it; and if a meadow or two presented itself and he pastured them in it, reward is written for him for what they consumed; and if they galloped a hill or two, reward is written for him for every step; and if a river presented itself and he watered them, he has for every drop they took into their bellies from it a reward, so much so that he mentioned reward in their dung and urine. And as for the one for which it is a cover: the one who keeps it for chastity, adornment and concealment, without withholding the right of their backs and bellies in ease and hardship. And as for the one upon whom it is a burden: the one who keeps it for insolence, arrogance, showing off to people, and regrets over it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and donkeys? He said: Nothing was revealed to me about them except this comprehensive, singular verse: (So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it). And this hadith was narrated by Suhayl and Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9081","9077 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Damrah Anas ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn 'Amir al-Aslami narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and morning came, he said: A listener has heard with the praise of Allah, His favor, and His good trial upon us; Our Lord, accompany us and bestow upon us."
"9082","9078 - Sa'id ibn Bahr narrated to us, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Two brothers presented a man to Madinah while a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had been struck in his body by an arrow; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his relatives: Seek someone to treat him. So the two brother-men were brought, and he said to them: Do you treat with iron? They said: No; we used to treat only in Jahiliyyah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Treat him. So they lanced it until he healed. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Suhayl except 'Asim ibn 'Umar."
"9083","9079 - 'Ali ibn Sahl al-Mada'ini narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, raising it (marfu'), he said: Whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one done to. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the hadith of Suhayl except from 'Asim and from Suhayl; and 'Ikrimah narrated it from Ibn 'Abbas."
"9084","9080 - Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man gives a morsel in charity from lawful earnings and places it in its right place, and Allah receives it with His right hand; it keeps growing until He raises it as one of you raises his foal, until it becomes greater than Uhud."
"9085","9081 - Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drought is not that you receive no rain, but drought is that the sky rains and the earth produces nothing."
"9086","9082 - And with it (the same chain) he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the sky rains a rain from which houses of mud-brick offer no shelter, and from which none offer shelter except houses of hair (tents)."
"9087","9083 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."
"9088","9084 - Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ubaydah al-'Usfuri narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are people who will come after me; one of them would wish to ransom seeing me with his family and wealth."
"9089","9085 - And 'Ali ibn Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs every day, a house will be built for him in Paradise: two before Fajr, four before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, two before 'Asr, and two after Maghrib."
"9090","9086 - And Yusuf ibn Wadih narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Habib narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say: The people are ruined; and whoever says: The people are ruined, he is the one who ruined them."
"9091","9087 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Kirmani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take my grave as an idol, and do not take your houses as graves."
"9092","9088 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Umar never took a path except Shaytan took a path other than it."
"9093","9089 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade a man to wear the dress of a woman and a woman to wear the dress of a man."
"9094","9090 - Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"9095","9091 - Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take your houses as graveyards; for Shaytan flees from the house in which Surat al-Baqarah is recited."
"9096","9092 - And with it (the same chain) he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a gecko on the first strike has such-and-such reward, and whoever kills on the second strike has such-and-such reward, and whoever kills on the third strike has such-and-such reward. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from the hadith of Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah."
"9097","9093 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A child does not repay his father except that he finds him enslaved and buys him and frees him. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9098","9094 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays after Friday, let him pray four."
"9099","9095 - Rizq Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns archery then forgets it, it is a blessing he has denied."
"9100","9096 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The expiation of a sitting is that a man says when he rises from it: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. This is his wording or its meaning. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain."
"9101","9097 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, from 'Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year."
"9102","9098 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, with the like of it."
"9103","9099 - I found in my book from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Abi Hazim informed me, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats us is not of us."
"9104","9102 - And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are no people who sit in a sitting then disperse without remembering Allah, but it is as if they dispersed from the like of the carcass of a donkey."
"9105","9103 - Yahya ibn Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-'Abbas: Among you are prophethood and kingship. And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman is weak; he narrated only this hadith."
"9106","9104 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Suhayl and al-'Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, raising it (marfu'): The best rows of men are the first of them and the worst of them are the last of them; and the best rows of women are the last of them and the worst of them are the first of them."
"9107","9105 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The poor came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the rich have gone with the highest ranks and lasting bliss. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is that? They said: They pray as we pray and fast as we fast, and they have wealth with which they give charity and free slaves, while we find none. He said: Shall I not guide you to a matter which, if you do it, none before you will precede you, and none after you will catch up with you, except one who does the like of what you did? He said: (Say) Glory be to Allah thirty-three times at the end of every prayer, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times. So they did; then that reached the rich, and they did the like of what the poor said. So they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we did what you commanded us, and they do what we do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the bounty of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from several angles."
"9108","9106 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees someone afflicted, let him say: Praise be to Allah who spared me from what He afflicted you with and favored me over many of those He created with favor; for when he says that, it is gratitude for that blessing. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this angle with this chain; and the scholars have accepted the hadith of Abd Allah ibn 'Umar."
"9109","9107 - Muhammad ibn al-'Ala narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah. And al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah - Suhayl raised it (marfu') - he said: The Euphrates will uncover a mountain of gold, and people will fight over it; of every hundred, ninety-nine will be killed. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Abu Hurairah, among them al-A'raj, Hafs ibn 'Asim, and more than one."
"9110","9108 - I found in my book from Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah al-Baghdadi, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, raising it (marfu'), he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, spoke to this western sea and spoke to the eastern sea. He said to the western sea: I shall carry in you servants of Mine; so how will you treat them? It said: I shall drown them. He said: Your harm is in your regions; He deprived it of ornament and hunting. And He spoke to this eastern sea, saying: I shall carry in you servants of Mine; so what will you do with them? It said: I shall carry them upon my hand; I shall be to them like a mother to her child. So He rewarded it with ornament and hunting. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, and he is munkar al-hadith (whose hadith is rejected); and Suhayl narrated it from al-Nu'man ibn Abi 'Ayyash, from Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, as mawquf."
"9111","9109 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not travel more than three days except with one who is unmarriageable to her (mahram). And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurairah from other angles."
"9112","Abu al-Zinad, from Abu Salih. 9110 - Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah, Blessed and Exalted, remains in the aid of a man so long as the man is in the aid of his brother."
"9113","9111 - And with it (the same chain) he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you puts on sandals, let him put on the right before the left, then begin removing the left before the right, until the right is the first of them to meet the sandal and the last of them to leave the sandal. And we do not know Abu al-Zinad to have narrated from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, except these two hadiths."
"9114","Salih ibn Abi Salih. 9112 - Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Zufar ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Abi 'Isa, from Salih ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise, their faces like the light of the moon on the night of full moon, without reckoning. So 'Ukkashah ibn Mihsan stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me of them. So he said: You are of them. Then a man of the Muhajirin, among their best, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me of them. He said: 'Ukkashah preceded you to it. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurairah from several angles; and we do not know it to be narrated from the hadith of Salih ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, except from the hadith of Abu Ma'shar from him."
"9115","9113 - Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, Malik ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None endures the hardship of Madinah - I think he said: - and its severity, except I shall be for him an intercessor - or a witness - on the Day of Resurrection."
"9116","9114 - Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Abi Nafi', from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prize race except in khuff, hafir or nasl (camel, horse or arrow)."
"9117","9115 - Wahb ibn Yahya narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"9118","9116 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from 'Abbad ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who performs wudu for prayer and washes his face except every evil he looked at scatters with the water - or with the drops of water; and he does not rinse his mouth except every evil his tongue uttered scatters with every drop of water; and he does not sniff (water) except every evil whose smell he found scatters - or comes out - with the drops of water; and he does not wash his hands except every evil he seized comes out with the drops of water; and he does not wash anything of his feet except every evil he walked to comes out with the drops of water. Then when he goes out to the mosque, a good deed is written for him for every step he takes, and an evil is erased from him thereby, until he reaches his place."
"9119","9117 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your oath is upon what your companion believes you in."
"9120","[Abu Bakr ibn Yahya], from his father, from Abu Hurairah. 9118 - Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Angels succeed one another among you, angels by night and angels by day, and they gather at the Fajr prayer and the 'Asr prayer; then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He asks them - and He knows best - Blessed and Exalted, saying: How did you leave My servants? They say: We left them praying, and we came to them praying. Then those who remained among you ascend to Him, and He asks them - and He knows best about you - saying: How did you leave My servants? So they say: We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying."
"9121","9119 - And with it (the same chain), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most lying speech; and do not spy, do not compete (in envy), do not hate one another, do not turn away from one another; and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"9122","9120 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels pray upon one of you so long as he remains in the place where he prayed, so long as he does not break wudu: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"9123","9121 - And with it, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: While a man was driving a garlanded sacrificial camel (badanah), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called to him: Ride it. He said: It is a badanah, O Messenger of Allah! He said: Woe to you, ride it. He said: It is a badanah, O Messenger of Allah! He said: Woe to you, ride it."
"9124","9122 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield; so when one of you is on a fasting day, let him not utter foul speech nor act ignorantly; and if a man fights him or reviles him, let him say: I am fasting."
"9125","9123 - And with it the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prophet among the prophets alighted under a tree, and an ant bit him; so he turned back, ordered his baggage, and it was removed from beneath it, and ordered it (the anthill) and it was burned with fire. So Allah, Exalted, revealed to him: Was it not a single ant?"
"9126","9124 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah; and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me. And these hadiths narrated by Abu Bakr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, have been narrated from Abu Hurairah from other angles; we mentioned them from this angle only to show that this man narrated from his father, from Abu Hurairah, these hadiths, even though they are with others."
"9127","Al-A'mash, from Abu Salih. 9125 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Sulayman - meaning al-A'mash - from Dhakwan - meaning Abu Salih - from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good deed a son of Adam does is (rewarded) tenfold up to seven hundred good deeds - or up to seven hundredfold. Allah says: Fasting is Mine, and I reward for it; the fasting person leaves food, drink and his desire for My sake; fasting is Mine, and I shall reward for it. And fasting is a shield; and the fasting person has two joys: a joy when he is about to break fast, and a joy when he meets his Lord. And the breath of the fasting person's mouth when it changes from food is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"9128","9126 - Ahmad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How much of the month has passed? We said: Twenty-two have passed and eight remain. He said: No; rather twenty-two have passed and seven remain; seek it tonight. Then he said: The month is twenty-nine."
"9129","9127 - Ahmad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Laylat al-Qadr was mentioned - or we mentioned it - in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How much of the month has passed? We said: Twenty-two have passed and eight remain. He said: No; rather seven remain. We said: No; rather eight remain. He said: No; rather seven remain; the month is twenty-nine."
"9130","9128 - Ahmad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress, Allah will relieve him of a distress of the Day of Resurrection; and whoever eases for one in hardship, Allah will ease for him in this world and the Hereafter; and Allah is in the aid of the servant so long as the servant is in the aid of his brother; and whoever travels a path seeking knowledge therein, Allah will ease for him a path to Paradise; and no people gather in a house of the houses of Allah, reciting the Book of Allah and studying it among themselves, except tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him; and whoever is slowed by his deed, his lineage will not hasten him."
"9131","9129 - Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi' and Abu Sawrah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever covers his Muslim brother, Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever relieves his brother of a distress of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress of the Hereafter; and Allah is in the aid of the servant so long as the servant is in the aid of his brother."
"9132","9130 - Ahmad narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Yahya Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it, and he added in it: And whoever grants respite to a Muslim (in a transaction), Allah will grant him respite from his stumble on the Day of Resurrection. And this phrase which Malik added, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, except Malik; and Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated it from Hafs, and he was not followed in raising it from Abu Hurairah."
"9133","9131 - Ahmad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me."
"9134","9132 - And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look to those below you, and do not look to those above you; for it is more fitting that you not disdain the favor of your Lord upon you. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from the hadith of al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurairah."
"9135","9133 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No wealth benefited us as the wealth of Abu Bakr benefited us. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except with this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash except Abu Mu'awiyah."
"9136","9134 - Amr ibn Ali and Yahya ibn Dawud both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, seek refuge with Allah from the trial of life and death, and seek refuge from the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"9137","9135 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; and when they say: There is no god but Allah, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, exalted is He."
"9138","9136 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters, he will have two rewards."
"9139","9137 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"9140","9138 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9141","9139 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Booty was not lawful for any black-haired people before you; a fire would come from the sky and consume it. Then on the day of Badr he said: The people hastened to take the booty, so Allah sent down: If it had not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took."
"9142","9140 - And with the isnad of Amr he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has an answered supplication, and I have reserved my supplication as intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection; every prophet hastened his supplication, and it will reach, if Allah wills, whoever dies not associating anything with Allah."
"9143","9141 - Amr ibn Ali and Yahya ibn Dawud both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is that which leaves sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand; your wife says: Spend on me or divorce me, and your slave says: Spend on me or sell me, and your child says: To whom do you entrust me."
"9144","9142 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me; if he remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself, and if he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better than them."
"9145","9143 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never crossed the heart of a human. Recite if you wish: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort for the eyes as reward for what they used to do."
"9146","9144 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor and the muezzin is one entrusted; O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."
"9147","9145 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor and the muezzin is one entrusted; O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins. And this hadith was narrated by Rawh ibn al-Qasim from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not mention al-Amash; and more than one narrated it from al-Amash who said: It was narrated to me from Abu Salih."
"9148","9146 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated it to us with it: Shuja ibn al-Walid and Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash who said: It was narrated to me from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah. And Nafi ibn Sulayman narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Aishah."
"9149","9147 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has angels, superfluous to the scribes of people, who roam about seeking remembrance - or about the earth - and seek out the people of remembrance; when they find a people remembering Allah, they call out: Come to what you seek. So they surround them with their wings up to the lowest heaven. He said: Then their Lord, while He knows best, asks them: What do My servants say? They say: They praise You, glorify You, and magnify You. So He, blessed and exalted, says: How would it be if they had seen Me? They say: If they had seen You, they would have been more intense in worship, more intense in praise of You, and more abundant in glorifying You. So He, mighty and majestic, says: What do they ask for? He said: They say: They ask You for Paradise. He said: So He, mighty and majestic, says: Have they seen it? They say: No, by Allah, they have not seen it. He said: So He says: How would it be if they had seen it? He said: They say: They would have been more eager for it, more ardent in seeking it, and greater in desire for it. He said: So He says: From what do they seek refuge? He said: They say: From the Fire. He said: So He, mighty and majestic, says: Have they seen it? He said: They say: No, by Allah, they have not seen it. He said: So He says: How would it be if they had seen it? He said: They say: If they had seen it, they would have fled from it more intensely, run from it more intensely, and feared it more intensely. He said: So He, blessed and exalted, says: I call you to witness that I have forgiven them. He said: Then an angel among the angels says: Among them is so-and-so who is not of them; he only came for a need. He said: They are companions with whom their companion does not suffer misery."
"9150","9148 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah - or Abu Said - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9151","9149 - And Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated it to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Said who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has roaming angels in the earth; when they find a people remembering Allah, they call out: Come to what you seek. Then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Jarir from al-Amash."
"9152","9150 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9153","9151 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness among the prophets before me is like that of a house which a man built and built well, leaving in it a single brick; so people come and look at it, saying: How beautiful this house is, if only this brick were completed! So I was that brick. And this hadith was narrated by Abu Muawiyah from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, and from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, separately."
"9154","9152 - And Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of you who will enter the Fire except that a man of the people of Paradise will inherit his place; that is His saying: They are the inheritors. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except with this isnad."
"9155","9153 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever believer I have insulted or flogged, make it for him purification and mercy."
"9156","9154 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced continuous fasting, and that reached the people, so they practiced it continuously; so he said: I am not like you; I remain with my Lord; my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"9157","9155 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then comes to Friday and listens attentively, he is forgiven what is between it and the (next) Friday, plus three days; and whoever says: Be quiet, has engaged in idle talk."
"9158","9156 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group to enter Paradise from my ummah will be upon the image of the moon on the night of the full moon; then those who follow them will be upon the brightest star in the sky; then after that ranks. They will not use cautery nor seek ruqyah; their combs will be of gold, their censers of aloeswood, their sweat of musk, and their temperaments upon the temperament of a single man, and the height of each of them sixty cubits."
"9159","9157 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright, draw near, and receive glad tidings; no one will be saved by his deeds. They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even you? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him."
"9160","9158 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the two-faced one."
"9161","9159 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will find the worst of the servants of Allah on the Day of Resurrection to be the two-faced one; the one who comes to these with the talk of these, and comes to these with the talk of these."
"9162","9160 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should fast on Friday except that he fasts a day before it or a day after it."
"9163","9161 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the most tender-hearted, and disbelief is from the direction of the East."
"9164","9162 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."
"9165","9163 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him lighten it; for among them are the elderly, the weak, and the one with a need."
"9166","9164 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at, nor purify, and for them is a painful punishment: a man with surplus water on a road in the desert who withholds it from the traveler, a man who pledges allegiance to a ruler pledging to him only for worldly gain - if he gives him he fulfills to him, and if he does not give him he does not fulfill to him - and the one who associates partners with Allah."
"9167","9165 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the son of Adam recites the verse of prostration, Satan withdraws weeping, saying: Woe to him; the son of Adam was commanded to prostrate, so he prostrated, and for him is Paradise; and I was commanded to prostrate, but I disobeyed, so for me is the Fire."
"9168","9166 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - while a funeral passed by him and he said -: How much did he leave? They said: Two dinars. He said: Two brands of Fire. He said: And whenever a funeral would pass by him, he would say: Is there a debt upon him? They would say: Yes. He would say: Did he leave enough to cover it? If they said: Yes, he would pray over him; and if they said: No, he would not pray over him. And this hadith is preserved only from the hadith of Jarir from al-Amash."
"9169","9167 - And with the same isnad he said: I would not love for Uhud to be turned into gold for me, with anything of it remaining with me after three days, except something I set aside for a debt; the wealthy are the fewest on the Day of Resurrection, except one who says: Like this, and like this, and like this - and few are they - to his right, to his left, before him, and behind him."
"9170","9168 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan hears the call to prayer, he turns away passing wind so as not to hear its sound; when it falls silent, he returns to whisper; when he hears the iqamah, he goes away so as not to hear its sound; when it falls silent, he returns and whispers."
"9171","9169 - And with the same isnad he said: When one of you is on a day when he is fasting, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly; and if someone acts ignorantly toward him, let him say: I am fasting."
"9172","9170 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises at night, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"9173","9171 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no newborn born except upon the fitrah until his tongue expresses; then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."
"9174","9172 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you; those before you were destroyed only by the frequency of their questions and their differing with their prophets."
"9175","9173 - Amr ibn Ali and Yahya ibn Dawud both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great, is more beloved to me than that upon which the sun rises. And we preserve these words only from the hadith of Abu Muawiyah from al-Amash."
"9176","9174 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between the two Blasts are forty. And I do not know whether forty days or forty years. And we do not know this hadith narrated as marfu with this isnad except from the hadith of Abu Muawiyah."
"9177","9175 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9178","9176 - And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and the wording is that of Abu Muawiyah - who said: Whoever kills himself with a piece of iron, his iron will be in his hand stabbing himself with it in his belly in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever; whoever poisons himself, his poison will be in his hand sipping it in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever; and whoever throws himself from a mountain, he will be falling in the Fire of Hell, abiding therein forever. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from the hadith of Abu Hurairah with this isnad."
"9179","9177 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the thief who steals an egg and his hand is cut off, and steals a rope and his hand is cut off. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except al-Amash from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah; and some of the people of knowledge interpreted that the egg is the iron helmet taken for war placed upon the head as protection, and that the rope is a rope carried by the Bedouins called a risha; and each of these two is worth more than a quarter of a dinar, and though the speech is general, this is its meaning, and Allah knows best."
"9180","9178 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"9181","9179 - Amr ibn Ali and Yahya ibn Dawud both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another; shall I not guide you to a matter which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread salam among you."
"9182","9180 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan ties three knots upon the nape of the head of one of you when he sleeps; if he rises and remembers Allah, a knot is loosened; when he rises and performs ablution, a knot is loosened; when he rises to prayer, all of his knots are loosened, so he wakes up energetic and good in spirit. But if he wakes and does not do that, he wakes up lazy, evil in spirit, having attained no good."
"9183","9181 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five prayers."
"9184","9182 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The breath of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk; the fasting person has two joys: a joy at his breaking of the fast and a joy when he meets his Lord; and every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is Mine and I reward for it."
"9185","9183 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede your imams in bowing or in prostration; when he says takbir, say takbir; and when he says: Not of those who earned wrath nor of those astray, say: Amin; for whoever's amin coincides with the amin of the angels, his past sins are forgiven; and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise."
"9186","9184 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loses his two beloved ones (his eyes), and is patient and seeks reward, I am not pleased with a reward for him less than Paradise."
"9187","9185 - Qumayr ibn Muhammad ibn Umayr narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And the hadith of al-Thawri, we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Abd al-Razzaq; this hadith was only known from the hadith of Jarir and Abu al-Ahwas, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah."
"9188","9186 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: What do you say in prayer? He said: I recite the tashahhud and remember Allah, then I say: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and seek refuge with You from the Fire; by Allah, I do not do well your murmuring nor the murmuring of Muadh! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muadh and I murmur around those two. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Jarir; and Abu Awanah narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih as mursal, and did not mention Abu Hurairah."
"9189","9187 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not to be withheld so that herbage may thereby be withheld."
"9190","9188 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast continuously from suhur to suhur. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Ubaydah ibn Humayd."
"9191","9189 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Adam and Musa argued; so Musa said to Adam: You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit; did you expel us - or expel your progeny - from Paradise? He said: So Adam overcame Musa in argument... and he mentioned the hadith."
"9192","9190 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah - or Abu Said."
"9193","9191 - And Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated it to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah - the two being close in their hadith - who said: When the expedition of Tabuk came, the people were struck by hunger, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would permit us to slaughter our riding camels so we may eat and take oil. He said: Do so. Then Umar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you do that, mounts will become few; but call them with the surplus of their provisions, then supplicate for them for blessing upon it, and perhaps Allah will place good in that - I think he said: good. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a leather mat, then called them with the surplus of their provisions; a man would come with a handful of corn, another with a handful of dates, another with a morsel, until it gathered upon the mat; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for them for blessing, and they left no vessel in the camp except that they filled it, and they ate and were satisfied. And a surplus remained. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I testify that there is no god but Allah; no servant meets Allah with it and is veiled from Paradise."
"9194","9192 - Ismail ibn Hafs narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray until his feet swelled; so he was spoken to about that, and he said: Shall I not be a grateful servant."
"9195","9193 - Isa ibn Abdullah, the nephew of Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli, said: My uncle Yahya ibn Isa narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"9196","9194 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd narrated it to us, Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray until his feet swelled, so it was said to him: Do you do that though Allah has forgiven you? He said: Shall I not be a grateful servant. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Thawri except Musa ibn Masud."
"9197","9195 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created creation, He wrote a writing, then placed it beneath the Throne: My mercy overcomes My wrath."
"9198","9196 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his wife and hastens and does not emit, there is no ghusl. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sufyan with this isnad except Musa ibn Masud."
"9199","9197 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, unless Allah envelops me with mercy and bounty from Him; and if He were to take me and Isa to account for what these two have earned, He would destroy us - and he pointed with the index and middle fingers."
"9200","9198 - Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything of the son of Adam decays except the tailbone. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Hafs."
"9201","9199 - Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Sad supplicating with two fingers and said: One, one. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Hafs; and others besides Hafs narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Sad."
"9202","9200 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Man has three hundred and sixty bones - or thirty-six joints - upon him is a charity every day. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who will not find? He said: He commands good or forbids evil. They said: Who cannot do that? He said: Let him remove a bone from the road. They said: Who cannot do that? He said: Let him guide the way. He said: Who cannot do that? Let him aid the weak. They said: Who cannot do that? He said: Let him withhold people from his evil. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Awanah."
"9203","9201 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Awanah."
"9204","9202 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no servant except that he has a reputation in heaven; if his reputation in heaven is good, it is placed upon the earth, and if his reputation is evil, it is placed upon the earth. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Waki."
"9205","9203 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."
"9206","9204 - Isa ibn Abdullah, the nephew of Yahya ibn Isa, said: My uncle Yahya ibn Isa narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they said to him: Shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Yes; are you harmed in seeing the sun and the moon? They said: No. He said: Then you will not be harmed in seeing Him - or you will not dispute in seeing Him - just as you are not harmed - or do not dispute - in seeing them. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Yahya ibn Isa; and this Yahya ibn Isa is a trustworthy man of the people of Kufah, of early rank."
"9207","9205 - Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated to us, Malik ibn Said narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was only sent as a gifted mercy. And we do not know anyone who connected it from Abu Salih from Abu Hurairah except Malik ibn Suayr; others send it, not saying: from Abu Hurairah, but saying: from Abu Salih, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9208","9206 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have intended to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then go with men carrying bundles of firewood to people who do not attend the prayer and burn their houses over them."
"9209","9207 - Isa, the nephew of Yahya ibn Isa al-Kufi, said: My uncle narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I have intended to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then go with men carrying tapers to people who do not attend the prayer and burn their houses over them."
"9210","9208 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub al-Tusi narrated to us, Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah is time. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Ammar ibn Muhammad."
"9211","9209 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qirats. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Ammar ibn Muhammad."
"9212","9210 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa and Amr ibn Ali both said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer has a beginning and an end; the beginning of the time of Zuhr is when the sun declines, and the end of its time is when the time of Asr enters; the beginning of the time of Asr is when its time enters, and the end of its time is when the sun yellows; the beginning of the time of Maghrib is when the sun sets, and the end of its time is when the horizon disappears; the beginning of the time of Isha is when its time enters, and the end of its time is when half the night passes; the beginning of the time of Fajr is when dawn rises, and the end of its time is when the sun rises. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Muhammad ibn Fudayl, and he was not followed in it; Zaidah ibn Qudamah only narrates it from al-Amash, from Mujahid as mawquf of his saying."
"9213","9211 - Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, Dawud ibn Sulayman Abu al-Mutarrif al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Malik ibn Suayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is a sanctuary between its two lava plains; whoever innovates an event in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. And we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except from the narration of al-Amash from him."
"9214","9212 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Malik ibn Suayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Said - raising it - who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says to His servant on the Day of Resurrection: Did I not carry you upon horses and camels? Did I not marry you to women? Did I not make you a chief who takes a fourth? Did you think you would meet this day of yours? He will say: No. So He will say: Today I forget you as you forgot Me. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Said except Malik ibn Suayr."
"9215","9213 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede your imams in bowing or in prostration; when he says takbir, say takbir; and when he says: Not of those who earned wrath nor of those astray, say: Amin; for whoever's amin coincides with the amin of the angels, his past sins are forgiven; and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise."
"9216","9214 - Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: And the recitation of dawn; indeed the recitation of dawn is witnessed. He said: The angels of the night and the angels of the day attend it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording from al-Amash except Asbat."
"9217","9215 - Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed the two rakahs of Fajr would lie down upon his right side. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad."
"9218","9216 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The prayer of one of you in congregation exceeds his prayer in his house and in his market by twenty-seven prayers; and that is because when one of you performs ablution and performs it well, then goes out to prayer intending nothing but prayer, nothing else moving him, he is raised a degree for every step and a sin is removed from him, until he enters the mosque; when he enters the mosque, he is in prayer as long as the prayer detains him, and the angels say: O Allah, bless him; O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him, as long as he does not break his ablution."
"9219","9217 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Muhadir - meaning Ibn al-Muwarri - narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so prays at night, but when morning comes he steals. He said: What you say will soon forbid him. And there is disagreement about this hadith: Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Jabir; and others besides Ziyad narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir; and Muhadir said in it: from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah."
"9220","9218 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me; if he draws near to Me a span, I draw near to him a cubit; if he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him running."
"9221","9219 - Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is prayed over by a hundred of the Muslims is forgiven. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah as musnad except Shubah."
"9222","9220 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us finds in himself something he would not be pleased to speak of, or that he fall from the sky is more beloved to him than to speak of it. He said: That is clear faith."
"9223","9221 - Shubah said: And Asim narrated to me, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"9224","9222 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man must not outbid his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Shubah, nor from Shubah except Abd al-Samad; and I think Abd al-Samad erred in it, for it is only known from the hadith of Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah."
"9225","9223 - Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah - raising it - who said: The pledged animal is ridden and milked. And we do not know anyone who raised it except Abu Awanah, nor do we know anyone who raised it from Abu Awanah except Yahya ibn Hammad and Shayban."
"9226","9224 - Mahmud ibn Khidash al-Talqani narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Muhammad, the brother of Ammar ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: And We prefer some of them over others in produce. He said: The sweet, the sour, and the sharp."
"9227","9225 - Ubaydullah ibn Usamah Abu Usamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And we do not know this speech narrated from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Sayf ibn Muhammad - and he is not strong; and the hadith of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Sulayman ibn Ayyub, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"9228","9226 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Madaini narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah."
"9229","9227 - And Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Adami narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Muhabbab Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever spends the night with grease upon his hand and something befalls him, let him blame none but himself. And this speech is not known narrated from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad and Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Amash."
"9230","9228 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad ibn Qumayr narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the one who drinks standing knew what is upon him, he would vomit."
"9231","9229 - Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Mamar."
"9232","9230 - al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about something, so he entered seeking something for him, and found a morsel in one of his rooms; so he brought it out, broke it into pieces, placed his hand upon it, then said: Eat, O Bedouin. So the Bedouin ate and a surplus remained of it; the Bedouin began raising his head, looking at him, and saying: You are indeed a righteous man. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Accept Islam - and he kept refusing Islam, saying: You are indeed a righteous man. And we do not know anyone who narrated this speech except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"9233","9231 - Abu Hisham narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Said al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them and said: What day is this? They said: A sacred day. He said: Then your blood and your wealth are sacred to you, like the sacredness of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. And this hadith was narrated by Abu Muawiyah from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah or Abu Said; and Abu Hisham combined them for us from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Said."
"9234","9232 - And with the same isnad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw a man pointing with two fingers and said: One, one."
"9235","9233 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi and Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim both said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban - meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman - narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The molar tooth of the disbeliever is like Uhud, and the thickness of his skin forty cubits. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Shayban."
"9236","9234 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given the keys of the treasures of the earth and they were placed in my hand. Abu Hurairah said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away - while you extract them or take them out. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Shayban."
"9237","9235 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no envy except in two: a man whom Allah has given the Quran and he recites it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, so a neighbor of his hears him and says: If I were given like what so-and-so was given, I would do in it like what he does. And a man whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it in truth, so a man says: If I were given like what so-and-so was given, I would do in it like what he does. And we do not know it narrated from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except with this isnad."
"9238","9236 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would one of you love, when he returns to his family, to find three large fat pregnant camels? We said: Yes. He said: Then three verses you recite are better for him than three fat large pregnant camels. And we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurairah except with this isnad."
"9239","9237 - Abdah ibn Abdullah al-Qasmali narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I was praying, then a man entered upon me and saw me, and that pleased me? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you are two rewards: the reward of secrecy and the reward of openness."
"9240","9238 - And Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And we do not know this speech narrated from the hadith of al-Amash except from the narration of Abu Waki and Said ibn Bashir."
"9241","9239 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, from his father, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I shall inform you of the affairs of people and their differences: A man who is quick to anger, quick to calm - neither against him nor for him - even; a man who is slow to anger, quick to be pleased - that is for him and not against him; a man who is quick to anger, slow to be pleased - that is against him and not for him. And the man who exacts what is his and pays what is upon him - that is neither for him nor against him; and the man who exacts what is his and delays people regarding what is theirs - that is against him and not for him. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Sharik, nor from Sharik except his son."
"9242","9240 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is given wealth by Allah and does not pay its zakah, there will be represented for him on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent with two spots, seizing his jaws, saying: I am your treasure. Then he recited: And let not those who withhold - the verse. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Sharik, nor from Sharik except his son."
"9243","9241 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer when he fornicates, nor does he steal while he is a believer when he steals, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it; and repentance is offered thereafter. And this hadith was narrated by Shubah from al-Amash with this isnad, and Abu Muawiyah also narrated it from al-Amash."
"9244","9242 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah - he said: and I do not know except that he raised it - that he disliked that a man put on sandals while standing. And we do not know it narrated from the hadith of al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except with this isnad."
"9245","9243 - Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The destruction of my ummah is at the hands of foolish young boys of Quraysh. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Shayban."
"9246","9244 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the five prayers is like a flowing river at the door of one of you in which he bathes every day five times; what then would remain of his dirt?! And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Muhammad ibn Ubayd; others besides Muhammad only narrate it from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir."
"9247","9245 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed by which I enter Paradise. He said: Do not become angry. He said: And another came to him and said: When do I know that I do good? He said: When your neighbors say that you do good, then you do good; and when they say: You do evil, then you do evil. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"9248","9246 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ablution is from what fire has cooked."
"9249","9247 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for a servant, so he said: Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than a servant?... and he mentioned the hadith."
"9250","9248 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid al-Shirazi narrated to us, Sad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call grapes al-karm, for al-karm is the Muslim. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Sad ibn al-Salt."
"9251","9249 - Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool the Zuhr prayer in intense heat. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Sharik, and he heard it only from Tamim, from Ishaq. Others besides Sharik only narrate it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said."
"9252","9250 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wore a shirt began with its right side."
"9253","9251 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah as mawquf; and Abd al-Samad ascribed it from Shubah, and Zuhayr followed him in raising it."
"9254","9252 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the first night of the month of Ramadan, the gates of Paradise are opened and the devils are chained. And Allah has freed ones at every breaking of the fast. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"9255","9253 - Ismail ibn Hafs al-Ubulli narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"9256","9254 - Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever catches a rakah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches a rakah of Asr - or two rakahs - before the sun sets has caught it."
"9257","9255 - Muhammad al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yunus informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is wounded with a wound in the path of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound as it was on the day he was struck, its color the color of blood and its scent the scent of musk."
"9258","9256 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Until one of them turns and a shin is uncovered, so they fall in prostration; and the backs of the hypocrites are fused until they become bone as if they were the horns of cows. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Awanah."
"9259","9257 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The poor of the believers will enter Paradise before their rich by five hundred years - or he said: by half a day. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"9260","9258 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah that they said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your ummah whom you have not seen? He said: Radiant from the traces of purification. And we do not know anyone who narrated it except this Mutarrif; Musa ibn Masud narrated it from him."
"9261","9259 - Yahya ibn Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: You will fight a people with broad faces and small eyes, as if their faces were hammered shields, and as if their eyes were the pupils of locusts; they wear hair footwear and take shields, tying their horses to palm trees. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Hibban ibn Ali."
"9262","9260 - Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asqati narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Musa ibn Uthman al-Hadrami narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark night, and with him were al-Hasan and al-Husayn; then lightning flashed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Join your mother. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Musa ibn Uthman; it is only known from the hadith of Kamil, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah."
"9263","9261 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not to be married upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Mindal."
"9264","9262 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women from the mosques. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of al-Amash from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abu Qutaybah, and he was not followed in it."
"9265","9263 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, both saying: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines; the best of them in Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they attain understanding. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Qays."
"9266","9264 - Sadan ibn Nasr narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bishr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except Abdullah ibn Bishr."
"9267","9265 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Said, the guide of al-Amash, narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever listens to the talk of a people while they dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this way, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Ubaydullah ibn Said."
"9268","9266 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor and the muezzin is one entrusted; O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you have left us competing over the adhan after you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be after me - or after you - a people whose lowest are their muezzins. And the beginning of this hadith was narrated by a group from al-Amash with their inconsistency in it and in its isnad; and the end of this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, and he was not followed in it."
"9269","9267 - Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the food of the two rivals in showing off. And we do not preserve this speech from the hadith of Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this way, and we heard it only from Uqbah ibn Mukram."
"9270","9268 - Abu Ghassan Rawh ibn Hatim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the night of the middle of Shaban, Allah forgives His servants, except for a polytheist or one holding grudges."
"9271","9269 - Rawh ibn Hatim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of the gardens and the gates of heaven are opened every Thursday evening, and deeds are presented therein; so Allah forgives therein every servant, except a polytheist, or a servant between whom and his brother there is enmity."
"9272","9270 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - while looking at the sun at its setting upon the edges of the palm fronds -: What remains of your day compared to what has passed of it? He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, what remains? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, what remains of the world compared to what has passed is but like what remains of your day compared to what has passed of it. And these three hadiths of Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman, we do not know anyone who shared them with him from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah; and this Abdullah ibn Ghalib is a man in whom there is no harm, and Hisham, we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Abdullah ibn Ghalib."
"9273","9271 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of yours, but he is content with the belittled deeds from you. And this hadith was narrated by Abu Ishaq from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah; and others narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, or Abu Said."
"9274","9272 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever invites you to food, answer him; whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him refuge; whoever does good to you, recompense him; if you cannot recompense him, supplicate for him until he knows that you have recompensed him. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah except al-Mughirah ibn Muslim; and I think he erred in it, for this hadith was narrated by Abu Awanah and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar."
"9275","9273 - And with the same isnad he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is three thirds: purification is a third, bowing is a third, and prostration is a third. Whoever performs it with its due is accepted from him, and the rest of his deeds are accepted from him; and whoever has his prayer rejected, the rest of his deeds are rejected. And this hadith is only preserved from the hadith of al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Kab as his saying; and we do not know anyone who ascribed it, saying: from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, and he was not followed in it."
"9276","9274 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad and Abu al-Musawir narrated to us, both saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather in the Fajr prayer and the Asr prayer; so they gather in the Fajr prayer - the angels of the night ascend and the angels of the day remain; and they gather in the Asr prayer - the angels of the day ascend and the angels of the night remain. Then their Lord, blessed and exalted, asks them: How did you leave My servants? They say: Our Lord, we came to them while they were praying, and we left them while they were praying; so forgive them on the Day of Judgment."
"9277","9275 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman - meaning al-Amash - from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites are the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer; if they knew what is in them, they would come to them even crawling; if one of you knew, when he came to them, that he would find a fat meaty bone of a sheep, or two good game pieces, you would all come to them; and I have intended to order the prayer to be established and order a man to lead the people, then order bundles of firewood and burn those men who did not witness the prayer today."
"9278","9276 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I would not love for Uhud to be gold for me, with anything of it remaining with me after three days except something I set aside for a debt; the wealthy are the fewest on the Day of Resurrection except one who says: Like this, and like this, and like this - and few are they - to his right, to his left, before him, and behind him."
"9279","9277 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never disparaged food at all; when it was brought to him, if he desired it he ate it, and if he disliked it he remained silent."
"9280","9278 - Ammar ibn Khalid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj - meaning Ibn Artah - from Ata, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a cupper, and the dowry of a prostitute."
"9281","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Waki' narrated, from Waki', from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it (i.e. the preceding narration)."
"9282","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Yahya narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra (with the same chain/content as above)."
"9283","And 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Take the pre-dawn meal (sahur), for indeed there is blessing in the sahur. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Abi Layla from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra, and Ibn Abi Layla also narrated it from 'Atiyya from Abu Sa'id, and he also narrated it from his brother from his father from Abu Layla; and the well-known version is the hadith of 'Ata from Abu Hurayra."
"9284","Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Maslama narrated, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no charity except out of self-sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"9285","Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Maslama narrated, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, in a raised (marfu') report, who said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created one hundred mercies, then He placed one mercy among them and divided it among His creation, and He withheld ninety-nine until the Day of Resurrection."
"9286","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Whatever was recited aloud to us we recite aloud to you, and whatever was concealed from us we conceal from you — meaning regarding the recitation in prayer."
"9287","Rizq Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated, al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and al-Hasan and 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer when he steals — I think he said: — nor does he plunder a plunder of high value while he is a believer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada combining Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and al-Hasan and 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Malik, and he was not a memorizer (not strong in memory), though a group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"9288","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The earnings of the cupper, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of the dog were forbidden."
"9289","Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Musa narrated, Mubarak ibn Hassan narrated, from 'Ata who said: Abu Hurayra narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The killer does not kill while he is a believer when he kills, nor does the adulterer commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer when he steals, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it, nor does he embezzle a booty while he is a believer; faith is stripped from him as a shirt is stripped off, then when he returns to faith it returns to him, and when he returns, faith returns to him."
"9290","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammam narrated, from 'Amir al-Ahwal, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except 'Amir al-Ahwal."
"9291","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, Harun al-Thaqafi, known as al-Barbari, narrated, he said: 'Ata narrated to me from Abu Hurayra (the text of the report follows in the preceding/succeeding narration)."
"9292","And 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra (with the same chain/content)."
"9293","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra (with the same chain/content)."
"9294","And Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Hammad narrated, from Ayyub, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made us hear, we make you hear, and whatever he concealed from us we conceal from you."
"9295","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: When you are an imam, lighten (the prayer), for among the people are the old, the weak, and the one with needs. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray the prayer in the cool (delay it from intense heat), for indeed intense heat is from the blast of Hell. And this hadith was narrated by other than 'Amr ibn 'Ali from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra as a stopped (mawquf) report."
"9296","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Both the cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"9297","And this hadith was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra as a stopped (mawquf) report; and 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated it from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra as stopped; and we do not know anyone who raised it (as marfu') from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman. Although there is disagreement from 'Ata: Ibn Jurayj and 'Abd al-Malik narrated it from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra, and Fitr narrated it from 'Ata from Ibn 'Abbas — thus Qabisa narrated it, while others than Qabisa sent it as mursal — and Layth narrated it from 'Ata from 'A'isha, and from 'Ata from 'Urwa ibn 'Iyad from 'A'isha."
"9298","Abu Nu'aym and Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated, from 'Isl ibn Sufyan, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-sadl (letting garments hang down in prayer). And this hadith was narrated from 'Isl by more than one, among them Hammad ibn Salama."
"9299","And 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar, from 'Isl ibn Sufyan, who said: 'Ata narrated, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Pleiades (the star) never rises while there remains any blight on earth except that it is lifted."
"9300","Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated, from Simak — meaning Ibn Harb — from 'Ata — meaning Ibn Abi Rabah — from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is asked about knowledge he has and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak ibn Harb from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except Ibrahim ibn Tahman, and we do not know Simak ascribed (marfu') from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except this hadith; and this statement was narrated from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra by Qatada, Malik ibn Dinar, and 'Ali ibn al-Hakam. As for the hadith of Qatada:"
"9301","Then Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated, al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated, from Qatada, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (with the same text: whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it...)."
"9302","And Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sadaqa ibn Musa narrated, from Malik ibn Dinar, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (with the same text)."
"9303","And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, as far as I know, he said: 'Umara ibn Zadahn narrated, from 'Ali ibn al-Hakam, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled with a bridle of fire. And the hadith of Qatada from 'Ata, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada except al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Malik. And the hadith of Malik ibn Dinar, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Malik except Sadaqa ibn Musa, and he is a Basran man, there is no harm in him."
"9304","And Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the people and said: O people, repent to Allah, for indeed I repent to Him one hundred times a day. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except Ibrahim ibn Maysara, nor from Ibrahim except Muhammad ibn Muslim."
"9305","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Raja and Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, they said: Hammam informed us, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour no Muslim servant coincides with asking Allah, Blessed and Exalted, for good except that He gives it to him. And we do not know Hammam ascribed (marfu') from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"9306","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated, 'Umar ibn Abi Husayn — and he is 'Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn — narrated, from 'Ata — meaning Ibn Abi Rabah — from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah did not send down any disease except that He sent down for it a cure."
"9307","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw in a dream as if my head was struck, and I saw it with this hand of mine; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan mocks one of you, then he goes in the morning narrating it. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except 'Umar ibn Abi Husayn."
"9308","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated, al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-sadl and that a man cover his mouth in prayer."
"9309","Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Baghdadi and Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, they said: Abu Nu'aym narrated, Ma'qil ibn 'Ubayd Allah narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Ma'qil once raised it (marfu') to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and another time stopped it short (mawquf), he said: Charity is out of self-sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. And we do not know Ma'qil ascribed from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"9310","'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, al-Hasan ibn 'Amr narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed I hear the voice of the child while I am in prayer, so I lighten it, fearing that his mother will be tempted (distressed). And this hadith we heard only from 'Ali ibn Sa'id from 'Abd al-Rahim from al-Hasan ibn 'Amr from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra; and this hadith is only known from the hadith of Talha ibn 'Amr from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra."
"9311","'Ammar ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not precede the month; fast at its sighting and break fast at its sighting — I think he said: — and if it is obscured for you then complete the number (of days). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Hajjaj from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi."
"9312","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Salama ibn al-Fadl narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I was given five things no prophet before me was given: the earth was made for me a purification and a mosque, and I was aided with terror against the enemy from a month's distance, and spoils of war were made lawful for me though they were not lawful for anyone before me, and I was sent to the red and the black though no prophet was sent except to his people, and no prophet but was given a gift which he hastened (in this world), while I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation."
"9313","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus ibn Muslim narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are an imam, measure the people by the weakest among them, for among them are the old, the young, the sick, and the one with needs; and when you pray by yourself, lengthen as much as you can."
"9314","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Humayd, the freedman of Ibn 'Alqama, narrated to me, 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him: Will you not graze in a meadow of the meadows of Paradise and rest therein? He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is grazing? He said: (Saying) praise be to Allah, glory be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. Salman said: Indeed everything has a planting, so what is the planting of Paradise? He said: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except with this chain, and Humayd, the freedman of Banu 'Alqama, we do not know anyone narrated from him except Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"9315","'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Humayd al-Makki, the freedman of the family of 'Alqama, narrated, from 'Ata — meaning Ibn Abi Rabah — from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"9316","'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Zayd narrated, Humayd narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed everything has a heart, and the heart of the Qur'an is Ya Sin. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths except Zayd from Humayd."
"9317","A man among our companions narrated to us, from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, he said: Humayd, the freedman of Banu 'Alqama, narrated to me, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and Ibn Mas'ud, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Nu'aym ibn Salama, a courier came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from an expedition he had sent, and Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not seen an expedition return quicker nor with more spoils than these; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, shall I not guide you to what returns quicker and is better in spoils? Whoever prays the dawn prayer in congregation, then remembers Allah until the sun rises. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except Humayd; and this Humayd, we do not know anyone who shared with him in these hadiths of 'Ata from Abu Hurayra."
"9318","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated, Talha — meaning Ibn 'Amr — narrated, from 'Ata — meaning Ibn Abi Rabah — from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Hurayra, visit occasionally and love will increase. Abu Bakr said: There is no authentic hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding (the saying) visit occasionally and love will increase."
"9319","And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has given you at your deaths a third of your wealth as an addition to your deeds. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ata except Talha ibn 'Amr and 'Uqba ibn 'Abd Allah al-Asamm, and both are not memorizers, and though a group narrated from them, they are not strong."
"9320","And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed I hear the voice of the child and I lighten (the prayer), fearing that his mother will be distressed."
"9321","And with the same chain he said: When you are an imam, measure the people by the weakest among them, and when you are the imam of yourself, then it is up to you."
"9322","Ahmad ibn al-Wazir narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated, Talha narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You will never encompass the people with your wealth, but what encompasses them from you is a cheerful face and good character. And Talha ibn 'Amr — our mention of his weakness has already preceded, so we have no need to repeat it afterwards."
"9323","Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated, Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Illicit gain (suht) is: the earnings of the cupper, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of the dog."
"9324","'Abd Allah ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated, Hammad ibn Salama narrated, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, with the like of it or close to it."
"9325","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Asim narrated, Hammad ibn Salama narrated, Budayl ibn Maysara narrated, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? They said: Yes. He said: The best of you are the best of you in character. And this hadith was narrated by other than 'Amr ibn 'Asim from Hammad from Budayl from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah as mursal (without the Companion)."
"9326","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another nor turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers. And this hadith, we heard no one narrate it from Abu 'Asim except 'Amr ibn 'Ali."
"9327","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Glorification (tasbih) is for men and clapping is for women. And this hadith we heard only from 'Amr ibn 'Ali from Abu 'Asim."
"9328","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (with the same content as above)."
"9329","And 'Abd Allah ibn Ishaq narrated it to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: He forbade the earnings of the cupper, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of the dog. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except Qays ibn Sa'd, Ibn Abi Layla, and Layth ibn Abi Sulaym."
"9330","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated, Hammad ibn Salama narrated, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: In every prayer there is recitation; whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made us hear, we make you hear, and whatever he did not make us hear, we do not make you hear. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qays ibn Sa'd except Hammad ibn Salama."
"9331","And 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu 'Awana narrated, from Raqaba, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra (with the same content)."
"9332","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated, Raqaba ibn Masqala narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: In every prayer there is recitation; whatever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made us hear, we make you hear, and whatever he concealed from us we conceal from you. And we do not know Raqaba narrated from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"9333","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubada narrated, Abu 'Amir al-Khazzaz — whose name is Salih ibn Rustum — narrated, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number; indeed Allah is Odd (Witr) and loves the odd. Do you not see that the heavens are seven, the earth is seven, the days are seven, the circumambulation is seven — and he mentioned other things. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu 'Amir from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra except Rawh ibn 'Ubada."
"9334","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated, Shu'ba narrated, from 'Abd al-Karim al-Mu'allim, from 'Ata who said: I saw Abu Hurayra saying the takbir when he rose and when he bowed down, and informing that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'ba except Abu Dawud, and Shu'ba did not ascribe (marfu') from 'Abd al-Karim al-Mu'allim except this hadith."
"9335","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed when the servant stands for prayer, he is only — I think he said: — before the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted; so when he turns aside, He, Blessed and Exalted, says: To whom do you turn? To one better than Me? Come to Me, O son of Adam, for I am better than the one you turn to. And this hadith was narrated by Talha ibn 'Amr from 'Ata from Abu Hurayra as stopped (mawquf)."
"9336","Tawus from him (Abu Hurayra). Salama ibn Shabib and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears and says, if Allah wills, has not broken his oath. And this hadith, I think Ma'mar abridged it from the hadith of Sulayman ibn Dawud who said: I will surely go around tonight to one hundred women, each woman among them giving birth to a boy who fights in the path of Allah; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he said, if Allah wills, and it did not happen, then he swore. So I suspect it became confused for Ma'mar when he abridged it, and Allah knows best."
"9337","And Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus narrated, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (the Sulayman narration that follows)."
"9338","And al-'Abbas ibn Yazid narrated it to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed Sulayman said: I will surely go around tonight to one hundred women, each woman giving birth to a boy who fights in the path of Allah; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he said, if Allah wills, every woman among them would have given birth to a boy who fights in the path of Allah. And there was born to him only from one woman, who gave birth to half a boy or part of a boy."
"9339","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who rode camels are the righteous women of Quraysh, the most affectionate to a child in his childhood, and the most caring for a husband regarding his wealth. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Tawus from his father from Abu Hurayra except from this route."
"9340","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for indeed suspicion is among the most lying of speech."
"9341","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, Jarir narrated, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it. And this hadith was narrated from Abu Hurayra from more than one route, and we do not know it narrated from Tawus from Abu Hurayra except from these two routes."
"9342","al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Had I been at the red dune, I would have shown you the grave of Musa (peace be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Tawus from Abu Hurayra except with this chain."
"9343","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated, Wuhayb narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Today there has been opened of the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this — and he made (the number) ninety (with his fingers). And this hadith, thus Wuhayb narrated it."
"9344","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated, and Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated it to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated, Wuhayb narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The two eyes commit adultery and the two hands commit adultery. Or he said: The adultery of the eye is the glance, and the adultery of the hand is the grasp, and the private part confirms that or denies it. And this hadith was narrated by Ma'mar from Ibn Tawus from his father from Ibn 'Abbas from Abu Hurayra."
"9345","Salama ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated, Zam'a narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray the noon prayer in the cool in intense heat, for indeed intense heat is from the blast of Hell. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Tawus from Abu Hurayra except with this chain from this route."
"9346","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated, Zam'a narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Regarding buried treasure (rikaz), a fifth. And this hadith we heard only from 'Amr ibn 'Ali from Abu Dawud from Zam'a."
"9347","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated, Zam'a narrated, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Upon every Muslim is a bath every seven days, and that is Friday."
"9348","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it or close to it."
"9349","Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa argued. So Musa said: You are Adam whom Allah created with His hand and breathed into you of His spirit; you removed us from Paradise — or: you removed your offspring — Adam said: And you are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech, so do you find that (written) against me before I was created? He said: Yes. He said: So Adam overcame Musa in argument."
"9350","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Imran ibn Aban narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the fitra (natural disposition), then his parents make him Jewish or Christian. And this hadith was narrated from Abu Hurayra from more than one route, and we do not know it narrated from Tawus from Abu Hurayra except with this chain."
"9351","'Umar ibn Shabba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar Abu al-Mutarrif narrated, Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, in a raised (marfu') report, he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, taught 'Isa (peace be upon him) his proof."
"9352","Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Adi narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubada narrated, Shu'ba narrated, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, in a raised report, he said: Upon every Muslim every seven days is a bath, and it is Friday. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'ba from 'Amr from Tawus from Abu Hurayra as raised except Rawh."
"9353","'Ali ibn al-Fadl al-Karabisi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, and Ibn Tawus from his father from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah led astray from Friday those before us, and Allah guided us to it. People are followers to us; for the Jews is Saturday, and for the Christians is Sunday. And this hadith, only Ibn Tawus raised it (marfu'), while the hadith of 'Amr is mursal; he did not say: from Abu Hurayra."
"9354","Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated, Sharik narrated, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be resurrected — and perhaps he said: people will be raised — upon their intentions. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it ascribing it (marfu') except Sharik from Layth, and other than Sharik narrates it from Tawus as mursal."
"9355","al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami and 'Ubayd ibn Bakhit narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Maslama narrated, Layth narrated, from Tawus and 'Ata, from Abu Hurayra, that he used to say the takbir whenever he bowed down and rose, and he said: I am the most knowledgeable of you regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9356","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to me, from 'Amr ibn Dinar who said: Tawus said, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is killed in blind partisanship ('ummiyya) with a stone or a stick, it is a mistake (killing), its blood-money is the blood-money of a mistake; and whoever is killed deliberately, it is retaliation (qawad); and whoever stands between him (the killer) and it (the retaliation), upon him is the curse of Allah and His anger; neither repentance (sarf) nor ransom ('adl) will be accepted from him. And this hadith was narrated by Sulayman ibn Kathir from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas."
"9357","Mujahid from him (Abu Hurayra). Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, 'Imran ibn Aban narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the riders (caravans bringing goods) before the market, and let not a townsman sell for a Bedouin; and whoever buys a musarrah (an animal whose udder was tied to inflate its milk), he may return it along with a sa' of food. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra except Muhammad ibn Muslim; and Muhammad ibn Muslim was narrated from by 'Imran ibn Aban and Abu Hudhayfa."
"9358","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, al-Husayn ibn Salih narrated, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat at the Ka'ba and drew his legs together, set them up, and embraced them with his hands (ihtiba). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra except Muslim, nor from Muslim except al-Husayn ibn Salih."
"9359","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated, al-Mas'udi narrated, Muzahim ibn Zufar narrated, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given five things no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, spoils were made lawful for me, the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification, I was aided with terror — I think he said: — and I was given the comprehensive words (jawami' al-kalim)."
"9360","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept advising me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir. Thus Yunus narrated it from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra; and Zubayd narrated it from Mujahid from 'A'isha; and Bashir Abu Isma'il narrated it from Mujahid from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9361","Muhammad ibn Firas Abu Hurayra al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Abu Qutayba narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade foul medicine. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this route; this wording is not preserved from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"9362","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (using) al-dubba (gourds), al-hantam (green jars), and al-muzaffat (pitched vessels for making intoxicants)."
"9363","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubada narrated, Shu'ba narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: He forbade al-dubba, al-hantam, and al-muzaffat."
"9364","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, and Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not meet the arriving goods (before the market), and let not a townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"9365","'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Mula'i narrated, from Layth — meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym — from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No servant believes until his neighbor is safe from his harms; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves the rich, forbearing, chaste one, and hates the foul-mouthed, sinful, begging, persistent one. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Layth from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra except with this chain."
"9366","'Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever loves the meeting with Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra except from this route with this chain; and it was narrated from Abu Hurayra from (other) routes."
"9367","Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah Abu Shayba narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Tabib narrated, Kamil ibn al-'Ala narrated, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery, let him lash her; then if she commits adultery, let him lash her; then if she commits adultery the third or fourth time, let him sell her even for a rope (of hair). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra except Abu Yahya al-Qattat, nor from Abu Yahya except Kamil. And it was narrated from Abu Hurayra from (other) routes."
"9368","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Samad al-'Ammi 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated, Mansur narrated, from Mujahid who said: Abu Hurayra and Ka'b met, and Abu Hurayra said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — or Abu Hurayra mentions from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — that he said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour no servant coincides with asking Allah therein for good except that He gives it to him. So Ka'b said ... and he mentioned speech we have no need to mention due to the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith was narrated by 'Ammar ibn Zurayq from Mansur from Mujahid from Ibn 'Abbas from Abu Hurayra."
"9369","Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated, Layth narrated, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in (the sura) When the sky is rent asunder (al-Inshiqaq)."
"9370","And with the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who perfumes herself and comes to the mosque to pray therein, Allah will not accept her prayer until she washes it off herself as she washes from major impurity (janaba). And these two hadiths, we do not know them narrated from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra except from this route."
"9371","Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Waddah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, my father narrated, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: There is none among the companions of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more preserving of his hadith than me, except 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr; for he used to comprehend with his heart and write with his hand, while I used to comprehend with my heart. And we do not know 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb ascribed from Mujahid except this hadith."
"9372","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are most severely tried? He said: The prophets, then the righteous. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mujahid from Abu Hurayra except Layth."
"9373","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Bakka'i narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated, Dhawwad ibn 'Ulba narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Send blessings upon me, for indeed it is a purification (zakat) for you, and ask for me al-wasila (the lofty station) in Paradise. So we asked him, or he informed us, and he said: It is a rank in the highest Paradise, and it is for one man, and I hope that I am that man."
"9374","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muzahim ibn Dhawwad ibn 'Ulba narrated, my father narrated, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Hurayra — (unintelligible foreign words: dardash kam) — I said: Yes, (I ransom you) with my mother and my mother (i.e. may my mothers be ransom). He said: Pray, for indeed in prayer there is healing."
"9375","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Salama narrated, Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated, from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: While a man was in a desert land, he heard thunder in a cloud; he said: Then he heard speech in the cloud: Water the garden of so-and-so, by name; so that cloud came to a watercourse and emptied its water into it. He said: So he went along with the cloud until he reached a man standing in his garden; he said: What is your name, O servant of Allah? He said: I am so-and-so — by his name — he said: So he said: What do you do with this garden of yours when you harvest it? He said: Since you said that, indeed I divide it into three thirds: I make a third for me and my family, I return a third to it (for expenses/seeds), and I make a third for the poor and the wayfarer. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route with this chain."
"9376","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salama al-Sukkari narrated to us, Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated, 'Ikrima ibn 'Ammar narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Adam and Musa (peace be upon them) argued; so Musa said to Adam: You removed the people — or: you removed your child — from Paradise; he said: So Adam (peace be upon him) said: You are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech, so do you find that written against me — I think he said: — before I was created? He said: Yes. He said: So Adam overcame Musa. This is his wording or close to it. 'Ikrima ibn 'Ammar said: And 'Abd Allah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"9377","Yazid ibn al-Asamm from him (Abu Hurayra). Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated, he said: I heard Yazid ibn al-Asamm narrating from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines like the mines of gold and silver; the best of them in ignorance (jahiliyya) are the best of them in Islam when they understand (the religion); and souls are assembled troops: those among them that recognized one another united, and those that disavowed one another differed."
"9378","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will surely ask you about everything, until they say: Allah created everything, so who created Him?"
"9379","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of wealth, but richness is richness of the soul; and by Allah, I do not fear for you mistakes, but I fear for you deliberate (sin); and I do not fear for you poverty, but I fear for you rivalry in abundance."
"9380","al-Walid ibn 'Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I have from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two pouches (of knowledge): I have narrated to you one of them; and had I narrated to you the other, you would have done to me, and you would have done... (i.e. you would have harmed/killed me)."
"9381","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Trials will appear, killing (harj) will increase — we said: What is harj? He said: Killing — and knowledge will be taken away. 'Umar said: I did not hear Abu Hurayra ascribe it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Indeed the taking of knowledge is not something snatched from the chests of men, but it is the passing away of scholars."
"9382","And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I intended to order the prayer to be established, then go out with young men carrying bundles of firewood, and burn down the houses of a people who hear the call and then do not come to the prayer."
"9383","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Mughira ibn Salama Abu Hisham narrated, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Asamm, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Have you seen His saying: And a garden whose width is the heavens and the earth — then where is the Fire? He said: Have you seen the night, how it covers everything — then where is the day? He said: Wherever Allah wills. He said: Likewise, wherever Allah wills."
"9384","Abu Kamil narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Asamm narrated, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he did not say: from Abu Hurayra (with the same text as above)."
"9385","Ahmad ibn 'Abda narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna informed us, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Asamm, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits could be seen — meaning from how he spread (his arms). Thus 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Asamm narrated it from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Abu Hurayra; and Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated it from Yazid ibn al-Asamm from Maymuna from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9386","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from Ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Asamm — and I think Abu Kamil narrated it to us from 'Abd al-Wahid from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Asamm — from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A blind man complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the loss of his sight and that he has no guide: Is there a concession for me not to come to prayer? So he permitted him, then he called him and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you hear the call? He said: Yes. He said: Then answer it."
"9387","And Marwan ibn Mu'awiya narrated, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Asamm, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah cursed the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"9388","al-Suhaymi from him (Abu Hurayra). Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus narrated, 'Ikrima ibn 'Ammar narrated, from Abu Kathir al-Suhaymi, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the text follows in the next narration)."
"9389","And Ibrahim narrated it to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated, Aban ibn Yazid narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated, from Abu Kathir al-Ghubari, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed wine is from these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine. And the name of Abu Kathir is Yazid ibn Udhayna."
"9390","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, that he said: By Allah, there is no believer who hears of me or sees me except that he loves me; so I said: And what is your knowledge of that, O Abu Hurayra? He said: My mother was a polytheist, and I used to call her to Islam and she refused me; so I called her one day and she made me hear regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I dislike; so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to call my mother to Islam and she refused me, and today I called her and she made me hear regarding you what I dislike; so supplicate Allah to guide the mother of Abu Hurayra. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, guide the mother of Abu Hurayra. So I went out running to give her glad tidings of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when I came to the door, it was ajar, and I heard the splashing of water; she heard the sound of my feet and said: O Abu Hurayra, stay where you are. Then she opened the door having worn her armor (dir') and hastened (without) her headcover, and she said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. So I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping from joy as I had wept from grief, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, rejoice, for Allah has answered your supplication; Allah has guided the mother of Abu Hurayra! Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me and my mother beloved to His believing servants, and to make them beloved to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make Your servant Abu Hurayra and his mother beloved to Your believing servants, and make them beloved to him. Abu Hurayra said: So by Allah, there is no believer who hears of me except that he loves me. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayra with this chain."
"9391","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus narrated, 'Ikrima — meaning Ibn 'Ammar — narrated, from Abu Kathir who said: Abu Hurayra narrated to me, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with Abu Bakr and 'Umar among a group of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from among us, and we feared he would be cut off from us; I was among the first to rush, so I came to the wall of a man of the Ansar and sought a breach but did not find one; there was a stream (rabi') emerging from its outer side, so I burrowed as a fox burrows, and entered. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Hurayra? I said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah. He said to me: What is the matter with you? I said: We missed you, so we panicked and feared you would be cut off from us, and the people calmed down, with Abu Bakr and 'Umar among them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go with these sandals of mine; whomever you meet behind this wall bearing witness that there is no god but Allah, his heart certain of it, give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: So I met 'Umar, and I said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go out with these sandals of mine; whomever you meet beyond the wall bearing witness that there is no god but Allah, his heart certain of it, give him glad tidings of Paradise. So 'Umar struck me a blow on my chest, and I fell on my backside; then I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what 'Umar did, while I was sobbing with weeping. So he said (to 'Umar): What made you do what Abu Hurayra says? He said: Abu Hurayra spoke the truth. He said: I fear for the people that they will rely (and abandon deeds). He said: Then leave them to work. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Kathir from Abu Hurayra."
"9392","Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated, Ayyub ibn 'Utba narrated, from Abu Kathir, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale have the choice as long as they have not separated. And this hadith was narrated from Abu Hurayra from more than one route."
"9393","Thumama ibn Hazn from him. Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated, al-Jurayri narrated, from Thumama ibn Hazn, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the dogs. So the people of Medina said: O Messenger of Allah, they benefit us; they are with our sheep and our crops. He said: Then kill of them the jet-black (al-bahim), and al-bahim is that about which people say it is the jinn."
"9394","Hammam from him. Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit."
"9395","Salama ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fire (injuries caused by fire/animals) is without liability (jubar)."
"9396","Salama ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was only named al-Khadir because he prayed upon a white fleece (farwa bayda) and it shook beneath him green."
"9397","Ahmad ibn Mansur and Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, he said: Ma'mar informed me, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was said to the Children of Israel: And enter the gate prostrating and say: Hitta (forgive us); but those who wronged said a word other than what was said to them; they said: A grain in barley, leaning back on their buttocks."
"9398","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated, Ma'mar narrated, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good word is charity."
"9399","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was stealing, 'Isa looked at him stealing, and he said: By Allah, I did not do it. He said: I believe in Allah, and I disbelieved my eyesight."
"9400","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight in the end of time a people of the non-Arabs, red-faced, flat-nosed, small-eyed, as if their faces are hammered shields, wearing hair (shoes/clothes). As for the hadith Fire is jubar, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayra, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from him except Hammam ibn Munabbih. As for War is deceit, Hammam ibn Munabbih narrated it from Abu Hurayra, and Abu Yunus, the freedman of Abu Hurayra. As for A good word is charity, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayra, and we preserve it only from the hadith of Hammam from Abu Hurayra. As for He saw a man stealing, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayra, and Hammam and 'Ata ibn Yasar narrated it from Abu Hurayra. As for He was only named al-Khadir because he prayed upon a fleece, this we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayra, and we preserve it only from the hadith of Ma'mar from Hammam. As for It was said to the Children of Israel: Enter the gate prostrating, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayra, and it was narrated from Abu Hurayra from another route."
"9401","Abu Maryam from him. Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated, Yahya ibn Abi 'Amr al-Shaybani narrated, from Abu Maryam, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wish I could be killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed — and he repeated it many times — when a man is wounded in the path of Allah — and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path — he will come on the Day of Resurrection with the color of blood and the scent of musk."
"9402","'Abda ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Mu'awiya ibn Salih narrated, from Abu Maryam, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man urinate in stagnant water and then perform ablution from it."
"9403","'Abda ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Mu'awiya ibn Salih narrated, from Abu Maryam, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trustworthiness (amana) is among al-Azd, and judgment or judiciary is among the Ansar. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayra with this chain."
"9404","'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Hibbani narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-'Abbas narrated, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, from Mu'awiya ibn Salih, from Abu Maryam, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with the forenoon supererogatory prayer (subhat al-duha), fasting three days of every month, and sleeping upon witr."
"9405","And with the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that a sheep be slaughtered and divided among the neighbors; he said: So I slaughtered it and divided it among the neighbors, and I gave the foreleg to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for the foreleg was the most beloved of sheep to him; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, 'A'isha said: Nothing remains with us of it except the foreleg. He said: All of it remains except this — meaning the foreleg (i.e. what was given in charity remains in reward)."
"9406","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises at night, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for indeed he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"9407","Malih ibn 'Abd Allah al-Sa'di, a Medinan. Yusuf ibn Salman narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Malih ibn 'Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The one who bows and rises before the imam — his forelock is in the hand of a devil. And we do not know Malih ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"9408","Tariq ibn Mahasin. Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated, from his uncle, he said: Tariq ibn Mahasin informed me, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was brought one stung (by a scorpion), and he said: Had he said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, he would not have been stung nor afflicted. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, and some of them said: from Tariq ibn Mahasin."
"9409","Ibn Hujayra. 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Shaybani narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Ibn Hujayra, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pay the zakat of your wealth, you have fulfilled what is upon you. And we do not know this statement narrated except from Abu Hurayra with this chain."
"9410","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Ibn Hujayra, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: Then indeed for him is a constrained life — he said: The constrained life which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, mentioned is that ninety-nine snakes are set upon him, biting his flesh until the Hour comes."
"9411","al-Dahhak. 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr narrated, he said: My father 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala narrated to me, from al-Dahhak ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first thing the servant will be held to account for is that it will be said to him: Did I not make your body healthy and quench you with cool water? And this statement, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route from Abu Hurayra."
"9412","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, as far as I know, from Yusuf ibn 'Atiyya, from 'Isa ibn Sinan, from al-Dahhak ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Arzab, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies in Bayt al-Maqdis, it is as if he died in the sky. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayra with this chain; and this Yusuf ibn 'Atiyya is a Basran, and he is not a memorizer, and he is old; he narrated from al-Hasan and Muhammad ibn Sirin."
"9413","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud. Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, al-Hajjaj — meaning Ibn Artah — narrated, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with al-Hasan and al-Husayn, one upon this shoulder and one upon that shoulder, kissing one at a time and the other at a time, until he reached us; a man said to him: Indeed you love them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me. And we do not know 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud narrated from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"9414","Salama ibn Qaysar. Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, from Ibn Lahi'a, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Abu al-Sha'tha, from Salama ibn Qaysar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts a day seeking the face of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire like the distance of a crow that flew as a chick until it died old. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayra with this chain."
"9415","Muhammad ibn Thabit. Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Bujayr narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated, from Musa ibn 'Ubayda, from Muhammad ibn Thabit, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Send blessings upon the prophets of Allah, for indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent them as He sent me."
"9416","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated, from Musa ibn 'Ubayda, from Muhammad ibn Thabit, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a man says to his brother: May Allah reward you with good (jazak Allahu khayran), he has excelled in praise."
"9417","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, teach me what benefits me, benefit me with what You taught me, and increase me in knowledge. Praise be to Allah in every state, and I seek refuge in Allah from the state of the Fire. And Muhammad ibn Thabit — we do not know anyone narrated from him except Musa ibn 'Ubayda, these three hadiths; nor do we know anyone who narrated them from Abu Hurayra other than him."
"9418","'Umara ibn Rashid. Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from 'Umara ibn Rashid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed among the worst of my nation are those nourished with blessings and whose bodies grew upon them."
"9419","And with the same chain he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Do the people of Paradise touch their wives? He said: Then he said: Yes, with a member that does not tire, a part that does not become worn, and a desire that does not cease. And 'Umara ibn Rashid — we do not know anyone who narrated from him except 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad; and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad was of sound mind, but he came upon unknown shaykhs and narrated from them rejected (munkar) hadiths, so his hadith became weak. And these two hadiths are among what was rejected against him, in which no one shared with him."
"9420","Damdam. al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Zayd Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated, 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Damdam ibn Jaws, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in the afternoon or noon prayer, and he stood in (after) the two rak'as; so they glorified (to alert) him, but he continued in his prayer; when he finished the prayer, he prostrated two prostrations then gave salutations. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording from Abu Hurayra except with this chain."
"9421","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated, 'Ikrima — meaning Ibn 'Ammar — narrated, from Damdam ibn Jaws who said: I entered the mosque of Medina seeking a companion of mine, and there I was before a man with shining front teeth, and beside him a dark-eyed, fair, handsome man, and they were in the shade of the mosque. He said: So the elder called me and said: O Yemeni. He said: So I came, and he said: Do not say: By Allah, Allah will not admit you to Paradise; by Allah, Allah will not forgive you. He said: I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: Abu Hurayra. So I said: O Abu Hurayra, by Allah you have criticized in me something I used to say to my family and servants when I was angry with them. He said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There were two men among the Children of Israel as brothers; one of them was diligent (in worship) and the other sinful. The diligent one would say to the sinful: Desist. So the sinful would say: Leave me with my Lord. Until one day he found him upon a grave (sin), so he said to him: Desist. He said: Leave me with my Lord; were you sent over me as a watcher? So he said: By Allah, Allah will not admit you to Paradise. So He sent to them an angel who took their souls; then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to the sinful: Enter Paradise by My mercy; and He said to the other: Were you capable over what is in My hand? Can you withhold My mercy from My servant? Take him to the Fire. Abu Hurayra said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He surely spoke a word that destroyed his worldly life and his hereafter. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayra from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain."
"9422","And with the same chain he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the noon prayer, and gave salutations after two rak'as and left; so Dhu al-Yadayn said to him: Was the prayer shortened, O Messenger of Allah, or did you forget? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither of that happened. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What does Dhu al-Yadayn say? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he bowed two rak'as, then gave salutations, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting, then gave salutations. And this hadith regarding the story of Dhu al-Yadayn was narrated from Abu Hurayra from (various) routes, and we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra with this wording except from this route."
"9423","Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Hisham ibn Abi 'Abd Allah narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Damdam, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered killing the two black ones in prayer — meaning: the snake and the scorpion. And this hadith was narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir by more than one."
"9424","'Abd Allah ibn Yamin. Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi narrated to us, Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn Muhabbab narrated, Sa'id ibn al-Sa'ib al-Ta'ifi narrated, from 'Abd Allah ibn Yamin, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the owner of the right (the creditor/debtor): Take your right with chastity (dignity), whether complete or incomplete. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hurayra except 'Abd Allah ibn Yamin, and I think he is Ta'ifi."
"9425","'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Mu'awiya ibn Salih narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed a mountain with Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, 'Ali, Talha, and al-Zubayr; the mountain shook with them, so he said: Be still, for upon you is only a prophet, or a truthful one (siddiq), or a martyr. And we do not know Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"9426","Salih ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Khalid ibn 'Amr al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Qabil, from Abu Hurayrah and 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, in marfu' form, he said: The upright among every generation shall carry this knowledge; they repel from it the distortion of the extremists, the interpretation of the ignorant, and the false ascription of the nullifiers. And this Khalid ibn 'Amr is munkar al-hadith; he narrated hadiths from al-Thawri and others which he was not followed upon, and this is among what he was not followed upon; we only mentioned it to clarify the defect in it."
"9427","Abu Salih al-Khuzi. 'Amr ibn 'Abdullah al-Awdi narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Abu al-Malih — meaning al-Farisi — narrated to us, from Abu Salih al-Khuzi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not ask Allah, He becomes angry with him."
"9428","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Waki' and Abu 'Asim narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And Abu Salih al-Khuzi was only called al-Khuzi because he used to reside in Makkah in Shi'b al-Khuz."
"9429","Abu Salih, freedman of Duba'ah. Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Kamil ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, from Abu Salih, and he is the freedman of Duba'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the onset of seventy and from the rule of boys. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Abu Hurayrah except this Abu Salih, and this Abu Salih — we do not know of anyone who narrated from him except Kamil."
"9430","Ahmad ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, may Allah have mercy on him, say: 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Kamil ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark night, and with him were al-Hasan and al-Husayn, then lightning flashed, and he said: Join your mother. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Kamil, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; and Kamil is not known except for a hadith narrated by Musa ibn 'Uthman al-Hadrami, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, and Musa was not followed upon it."
"9431","Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Kamil ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: the witr before sleep, the two rak'ahs of Duha, and that I not sleep except upon witr. And Kamil narrated other hadiths from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; among them is what we have mentioned, and among them is what he narrated: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise except one who refuses; and among them: The Hour shall not come until the world — or it becomes — belongs to Luka' ibn Luka'. And this is munkar."
"9432","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Harun ibn 'Antarah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: the witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and that I not sleep except upon witr. And we do not know of 'Antarah narrating from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it except 'Abd al-Malik ibn Harun, from his father, from his grandfather. And 'Abd al-Malik is lenient in hadith, and his father is trustworthy."
"9433","And Muhammad ibn Wasi' narrated from Ma'ruf, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things. Then he mentioned something similar, and it is among what Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi', from Ma'ruf, from Abu Hurayrah, with this hadith."
"9434","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Ali said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrating from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you differ about the road, make it seven cubits. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Jarir ibn Hazim; and Ayyub followed Jarir ibn Hazim and narrated it from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah; and Simak ibn Harb narrated it from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"9435","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrating from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall. And this hadith — thus Ayyub and al-Zubayr narrated it from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah; and Jabir ibn Yazid narrated it from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas."
"9436","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrating from 'Utbah al-Kufi — and in my view he is 'Utbah ibn Yaqzan — from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finds a louse in the mosque, let him bury it. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the narration of Abu Hurayrah with this chain, and 'Utbah ibn Yaqzan is well known; a group narrated from him."
"9437","Yahya ibn Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: He forbade a man, when he puts on sandals, to begin with the left before the right, and he said: Let him take them both off together — or let him put them both on together. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other chains with more complete wording than this, and we do not know it narrated from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, except through this chain."
"9438","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from 'Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The fornicator does not fornicate while he fornicates while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he steals while he is a believer, nor does he plunder a plunder of high value while he is a believer. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), through other chains, and we do not know it narrated from the hadith of 'Ikrimah from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain, and 'Ikrimah did not narrate from Ibn 'Umar except this hadith."
"9439","'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn Usayd al-Bahili narrated to us, 'Abbad — meaning Ibn 'Abbad al-Muhallabi — narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Ali, and he was asked about the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The fornicator does not fornicate while he fornicates while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he steals while he is a believer. He said: So he drew a wide circle on the ground, then drew a circle in the middle of the circle, and said: The first circle is Islam, and the circle in the middle of the circle is faith; so when he fornicates he exits from faith to Islam, and nothing expels him from Islam except shirk."
"9440","'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq. Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Budayl, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave and from the punishment of Hell and the false messiah, the Dajjal. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Budayl except Shu'bah."
"9441","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes up, let him not dip his hand into his vessel until he has washed it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq except Khalid, and it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other paths."
"9442","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us, from Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as though he were your companion, and I saw Musa (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tall and dark-skinned, and I saw 'Isa (peace be upon him) red-complexioned and curly-haired. And this hadith has been narrated by others besides 'Ali from Khalid."
"9443","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: Ibn 'Abbas addressed us one day after 'Asr until the sun set and the stars appeared, and the people kept calling out to him: The prayer, the prayer; and among the people was a man from Banu Tamim. Ibn 'Abbas said: Do you teach me the Sunnah? May you have no mother. I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combine Zuhr and 'Asr and Maghrib and 'Isha. He said: So I met Abu Hurayrah and he agreed with him. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from the hadith of 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn 'Abbas and Abu Hurayrah, except from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq; and we do not know of al-Zubayr narrating in musnad form from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9444","Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd al-Hunai. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd al-Hunai narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was between Dajnan and 'Usfan, and the polytheists said: These people have a prayer dearer to them than their fathers and their sons, and it is the 'Asr prayer; so combine your affair and incline upon them in one assault. And Jibril (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and commanded him to divide his companions into two halves: he prays with one half, and the other party stands behind them, and these take their precaution and their weapons; so there shall be for them one rak'ah each, and for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rak'ahs. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, except Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd, nor from Sa'id except 'Abd al-Samad."
"9445","'Abdah ibn 'Abdullah and Ahmad ibn Mansur said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Bara' ibn Yazid informed us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu' form, he said: Shall I not tell you of the people of Paradise? The weak, the wronged. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? Every coarse arrogant one. Shall I not inform you of the best of you? The best of you in manners. Shall I not inform you of the worst of you? The chatterers, the pretentious in speech, the pompous. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain, and it has been narrated from others besides Abu Hurayrah."
"9446","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Nizar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jallalah — the animal feeding on filth — and forbade drinking its milk and eating it and riding it. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain with this isnad; and Ash'ath ibn Nizar is lenient in hadith, Basran."
"9447","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Nizar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are told a hadith from me and it agrees with the truth, then I said it. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Ash'ath, and we have already mentioned his weakness."
"9448","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels do not accompany a company among whom is a bell. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from 'Aishah."
"9449","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya and Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, 'Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever strikes with a lash unjustly shall be retaliated upon him on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Raja', from 'Imran, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9450","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Laylat al-Qadr is the night of the twenty-seventh or twenty-ninth, and the angels on those nights on earth are more numerous than the number of pebbles. And we do not know of Qatadah narrating from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, except these two hadiths, nor do we know for them a path from Abu Hurayrah except this path we mentioned."
"9451","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Hilal ibn Usamah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband divorced me and he wants to snatch my son from me, and he has already drawn water for me from the well of Abu 'Inabah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O boy, this is your mother and this is your father; so he gave him the choice between his father and his mother."
"9452","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated it to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Maymunah, he said: I witnessed Abu Hurayrah giving a boy the choice between his father and his mother, and he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving a boy the choice between his father and his mother."
"9453","Mutarrif ibn 'Abdullah. Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad — meaning Ibn Salamah — narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu al-'Ala', from Mutarrif, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about lost property, and he said: It is to be announced, neither concealed nor hidden; if its owner comes, otherwise it is Allah's property which He gives to whom He wills. And we do not know of Mutarrif narrating in musnad form from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9454","Bashir ibn Nuhayk. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning a slave jointly owned between two men when one of them frees his share, he said: He guarantees the share of his partner if he is well-off."
"9455","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning a man who goes bankrupt and a man finds his goods intact with him, he said: He has more right to them."
"9456","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gold ring. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah through a better chain than this chain."
"9457","And with the same chain, he said: 'Umra — a life grant — is permissible. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain."
"9458","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu 'Imran Musa ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has servants who are neither prophets nor martyrs; the prophets and martyrs shall envy them on the Day of Resurrection."
"9459","'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Huraym narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every child is born upon the fitrah; then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian."
"9460","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Barakah, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"9461","Abu Ayyub al-Azdi. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face. Mudarib ibn Hazn."
"9462","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Bashir ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Mudarib ibn Hazn, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no 'adwa — contagion by itself — and no hamah, and the best of omens is the good omen, and the evil eye is real. And we do not know of Mudarib narrating from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9463","Abu al-Jawza'. 'Amr ibn 'Ali and Muhammad ibn Bashshar said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Jawza', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the believer is taken, the angels of mercy take him, and his soul is delivered in white silk; he is carried up to heaven, and they say: We have not found a fragrance more pleasant than this. And they say: Leave him to rest, for he was in the grief of the world. And they say: What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? Until they reach heaven with him. As for the disbeliever, when he is taken, the keepers say: We have not found a stench fouler than this; then they proceed with him to the lowest earth. And this hadith was narrated by Hisham from Qatadah, from Qasamah, from Abu Hurayrah, and it has a better wording."
"9464","Sa'd ibn Hisham. 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Hisham, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dog, the donkey, and the woman cut off the prayer. And we do not know of Sa'd ibn Hisham narrating from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9465","Anas ibn Hakim. Ahmad narrated to us, he said: I found in my book, from Muhammad ibn Marzuq: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Aban — meaning Ibn Yazid — from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Hakim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant shall be held to account for is his prayer; if it is sound, he has succeeded and prospered, and if it is bad, he has failed and lost. And this hadith — we do not know of a path from Abu Hurayrah better than this path."
"9466","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Yunus, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Hakim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"9467","'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus — meaning Ibn 'Ubayd — from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ziyad ibn Matar, from Abu Hurayrah. Thus Sufyan narrated it from Yunus; and Hammad said: From Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ziyad ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9468","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ziyad ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever leaves obedience and parts from the community and dies upon that, his death is a death of ignorance; and whoever goes out against my ummah striking its righteous and its wicked, showing no restraint — or he said: not holding back — from its believer nor fulfilling the covenant of its covenanted ones, he is not of my ummah; and whoever is killed under a blind banner, angered for partisanship, his killing is a killing of ignorance. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah through this chain."
"9469","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the month of Ramadan, a blessed month; Allah has obligated its fasting; in it the gates of Paradise are opened and the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained; and in it is a night better than a thousand months; whoever is deprived of it has been deprived. And this hadith has been narrated from Ayyub by more than one."
"9470","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, 'Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-'Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is a brick of gold and a brick of silver, and its mortar is musk."
"9471","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever enters Paradise enjoys bliss and never suffers misery; he lives and never dies; his clothes never wear out, and his youth never perishes. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Hisham; and 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr is Basran, not well known; we do not know of anyone who narrated from him except Qatadah; and this wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other chains."
"9472","Muhammad ibn Ziyad. 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right; and when he takes them off, let him begin with the left; or let him take them both off together or put them both on together."
"9473","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seventy thousand of my ummah shall enter Paradise without reckoning. Then a man stood and said: Supplicate to Allah to make me among them. He said: O Allah, make him among them. Then another man stood and said: Supplicate to Allah to make me among them. He said: 'Ukkashah has preceded you to it."
"9474","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The poor one is not the itinerant beggar whom a date or two dates, or a morsel or two morsels, turn away; but the poor one is he who finds no sufficiency and does not ask people importunately."
"9475","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"9476","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim say: When one's servant comes to one of you with his food, having borne — I think he said — its heat and its smoke, or a word similar to it — I think he said — then let him seat him with him; and if he does not seat him with him, let him give him some of his food."
"9477","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels — or the ankles — from the Fire."
"9478","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The changed breath of the fasting one's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"9479","And with the same chain, he narrates from his Lord, blessed and exalted be He, He said: Every deed is expiation, and fasting is Mine and I reward for it."
"9480","And with the same chain, he says: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with, asking Allah therein for something, except He gives it to him."
"9481","And with the same chain: The child belongs to the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone."
"9482","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — I think he said —: A woman tied up her cat; she neither fed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth, so it died; so Allah admitted her to the Fire."
"9483","Talut ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mine is exempt from liability, and the well is exempt from liability, and the beast is exempt from liability; and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"9484","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you put on sandals, begin with the right; and when you take them off, begin with the left; or take them both off together, or put them both on together."
"9485","And with the same chain: The child belongs to the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone."
"9486","'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar, freedman of Banu Hashim. 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its people shall be cast into the Fire and it shall say: Is there more? Until He, blessed and exalted be He, comes to it and places His foot in it; then it shall contract and say: Enough, enough."
"9487","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People are mines in good and evil; the best of them in ignorance are the best of them in Islam when they gain understanding."
"9488","And with the same chain, he said: When the servant of one of you comes to him with his food, having borne its heat and its labor, and he does not seat him with him to eat, let him give him a morsel of his food."
"9489","'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from 'Ammar, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9490","He said: And I am Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam met Musa (peace be upon them both), and he said: Are you Adam whom Allah created with His hand and settled in His garden and made His angels prostrate to you and breathed into you of His spirit; then you did what you did and expelled your offspring from Paradise? So Adam said: Are you Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and spoke to and gave the Torah and brought near as a confidant? He said: Yes. He said: So am I older or is the Decree? He said: The Decree. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa; so Adam overcame Musa. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from 'Ammar except Hammad ibn Salamah; and 'Ammar is a man of Basra, well known; Yunus ibn 'Ubayd and Khalid al-Hadhdha' and 'Ali ibn Zayd and Hammad ibn Salamah and others narrated from him."
"9491","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar and Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men shall leave Madinah out of aversion to it, though Madinah is better for them if they knew."
"9492","Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, Badal ibn al-Muhabbir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Sulayman al-Taymi, from Bakr, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in: When the sky is split asunder."
"9493","And Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated it to us: Badal narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah and Marwan al-Asghar, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"9494","Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Yunus, from Bakr, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith has been narrated from Yunus by more than one."
"9495","And Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated it to us: 'Abd al-Qahir narrated to us, from Hisham; and Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated it."
"9496","Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, 'Imran — meaning al-Qattan — narrated to us, from Bakr ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man remains in prayer so long as he is in his place of prayer, so long as he does not break his ablution."
"9497","Muhammad ibn Shu'bah ibn Juwan narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sa'id — meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah — narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Julas, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays one rak'ah of the dawn prayer before the sun rises and it rises, let him pray another to it."
"9498","Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Razin narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Julas, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr in faith and seeking reward, his past sins shall be forgiven. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Sa'id except 'Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Razin, and he was trustworthy. And it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other chains."
"9499","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, and from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the fasting one are two joys: a joy in this world at his breaking fast, and a joy in the Hereafter."
"9500","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Zakariyya (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a carpenter. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"9501","Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah. Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Awf, he said: I heard Khilas say: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three men went out seeking provision for their families; rain seized them, so they took refuge in a cave; a rock fell upon them from the mouth of the cave and blocked the mouth of the cave against them. The men said to one another: The trace is effaced, the rock has fallen, and none knows your place but Allah Almighty; so come, let each man of you supplicate with the most firmly established deed he ever did for Allah Almighty, hoping He may bring you out of your place. One of them said: O Allah, if You know that I was dutiful to my parents, and that I would bring my sheep home in the evening, and I would milk for my parents and bring it to them while they lay upon their bed, until I gave them drink with my hand; and one night I came to them with their drink and found them asleep, and I kept waiting in their sleep, disliking to wake them, and disliking to return with the drink lest they wake and not find me with them; so I stood in my place standing over their heads thus until morning. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your face, then relieve us. He said: So a third of the rock moved away. They said to the next: O man. So the second said: O Allah, if You know that I loved a cousin of mine with intense love, and I proposed to her to her family but they refused me, until I offered her what she agreed upon between me and her; then I called for her and was alone with her, and I sat from her as a man sits from a woman; and she said: It is not lawful for you to break the seal except by its right. So my soul recoiled, and I honored her right. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your face, then relieve us. He said: So the rock moved away, and they said to the third: Come, speak. The third said: O Allah, if You know that a worker worked for me for a sa' of food, then the worker left without taking his sa'; it remained withheld with me for a long time, and I took to his sa' and kept cultivating it until there gathered from that sa' many cattle, many sheep, and much wealth; and that worker came to me after a time seeking the sa' of food, and I said to him: That sa' of yours of food has become much wealth, many sheep, and many cattle; so take all this, for it is from that sa'. He said to me: Are you mocking me? I said to him: No, by Allah, but it is the truth. So he left with it driving all the wealth. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your face, then relieve us. So the rock split and fell, and they went out walking. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from 'Awf from Khilas except al-Mu'tamir."
"9502","Muhammad ibn 'Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, Qabisah ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Awf, from Khilas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not for the Children of Isra'il, meat would not have spoiled; and were it not for Hawwa', no female would have betrayed her husband. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayrah, nor did anyone narrate it from Abu Hurayrah except Khilas."
"9503","'Abdullah ibn Rabah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sulayman — meaning Ibn al-Mughirah — narrated to us, from Thabit, from 'Abdullah ibn Rabah, he said: A delegation came to Mu'awiyah, may Allah have mercy on him, and I was among them, and Abu Hurayrah; and that was in Ramadan. Some of us would prepare food for others, and Abu Hurayrah was among those who did so often, inviting to his lodging. So I said: Shall I not prepare food and invite them to my lodging? He said: Then I met Abu Hurayrah in the evening. He said: I said: The invitation is with me tonight. He said: Have you preceded me? I said: Yes. So I invited them and they were with me, and Abu Hurayrah said: Shall I not inform you of a hadith from your hadith, O company of Ansar? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he entered Makkah. He said: He sent al-Zubayr upon one of the two flanks, and sent Khalid ibn al-Walid upon the other flank, and sent Abu 'Ubaydah upon the unarmed — and the unarmed are those without armor — and Quraysh had gathered their rabble and followers. They said: We put these forward; if they prevail we live with them, and if they are struck we give. They took the belly of the valley, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a battalion. He looked and saw me, and said: O Abu Hurayrah. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you see the rabble of Quraysh and their followers? Then he said: Call the Ansar, and let none come to me except an Ansari. So he called them and they came until they surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Do you see the rabble of Quraysh and their followers? Then he struck one hand upon the other and said: Mow them down until you meet me at al-Safa. Abu Hurayrah said: So we set out, and none of us wished to kill any of them he wished except he did. And Abu Sufyan came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the multitude of Quraysh has been made lawful; there shall be no Quraysh after today. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever closes his door is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe. He said: So the people closed their doors. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he reached the Stone and touched it, then circumambulated the House, and in his hand was a bow held by its grip; he came upon an idol beside the House and began striking its eye with it, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished. Then he went on until he came to al-Safa where he could see the House; he raised his hands and began praising Allah and supplicating, while the Ansar were beneath him, some saying to others: As for the man, longing for his people has seized him and compassion for his kin. He said: And Abu Hurayrah said: And revelation came, and when it came it was not hidden from them; no one raises his glance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until the revelation ends. When the revelation ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, did you say: As for the man, longing for his kin has seized him and compassion for his clan? They said: We did say that. He said: No indeed; I am Allah's servant and His messenger; I emigrated to Allah and to you; life is your life, and death is your death. So they came to him weeping, saying: By Allah, we said what we said only out of protectiveness for Allah and His messenger. He said: Allah and His messenger believe you and excuse you."
"9504","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-'Ala' ibn Ziyad al-'Adawi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is a brick of gold and a brick of silver."
"9505","Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Abu Hurayrah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym and Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hakim al-Athram, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to a soothsayer and believes him in what he says, or comes to a menstruating woman, or comes to a woman in her rear, has disavowed what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith — we do not know it narrated with this wording except Hakim al-Athram, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Hurayrah; and Hakim is munkar al-hadith; his hadith is not used as proof when he is alone with it, and this is among what he was alone with."
"9506","Bushayr ibn Ka'b. 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Bushayr ibn Ka'b, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you dispute about the road, make it seven cubits. And we do not know of Bushayr ibn Ka'b narrating from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9507","'Abbas al-Jushami. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Abbas al-Jushami, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the Qur'an there is a surah of thirty verses which interceded for its companion until he was forgiven: Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion, and He is over all things competent."
"9508","Al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, may Allah be pleased with him, mention it from 'Amr ibn Marzuq, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from 'Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad."
"9509","'Uthman ibn Shammas. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Julas, he said: I heard 'Uthman ibn Shammas, a man of his people, say: Sa'id ibn al-'As sent me to Madinah. He said: So I was with Marwan, and Abu Hurayrah passed by, and he said: Some of your hadith, O Abu Hurayrah. Then he went on, then came back to him, and we said: Now he will attack him. Then he said: How did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over the funeral? He said: You created it — or him — and You guided it to Islam, and You took its soul; You know its secret and its open; we have come to You as intercessors, so forgive it."
"9510","'Ali ibn Shammakh. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: And Musaddad narrated to us: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abu al-Julas 'Uqbah ibn Sayyar, from 'Ali ibn Shammakh, he said: I witnessed Marwan ask Abu Hurayrah: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over the funeral? He said: O Allah, You are its Lord, You created it, You guided it, and You know best its secret and its open; we have come as intercessors, so forgive it. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah with this wording except with this isnad."
"9511","Bishr ibn Harb. Ibrahim narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad — meaning Ibn Salamah — narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Abu Hurayrah, that two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and he said: Go to these mountain paths, gather firewood and sell it. So they went and gathered firewood, then came and sold it and obtained food; then they went and gathered firewood again and came; they kept on until they bought two garments, then bought two donkeys. Then they said: Allah has blessed for us the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9512","Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said — and I do not think it but from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — he said: The poor of this ummah shall enter before its rich by forty years."
"9513","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Beware of suspicion, for it is the falsest of speech; do not spy, do not hate one another, do not break ties, do not turn away from one another; and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"9514","Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu' form, he said: A man among those before you bought a property from a man and found therein a jar of gold. He said to him: I only bought the property from you, I did not buy the gold from you. The seller said: I only sold you the property with what is in it. He said: So they sought judgment from one of those living at that time, and he said to one of them: Do you have a daughter? And said to the other: Do you have a son? They said: Yes. He said: Then marry one to the other, and let them spend upon themselves from this wealth. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who raised it in marfu' form from Sulaym from Abu Hurayrah."
"9515","Sa'id ibn Mina. Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Mina, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The changed breath of the fasting one's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"9516","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you is fasting, let him not engage in obscenity that day nor act ignorantly; and if a man fights him or insults him, let him say: I am fasting."
"9517","Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman. Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Abu Hisham al-Mughirah ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Dawud — meaning al-Awdi — from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate into stagnant water and then perform ablution from it."
"9518","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — meaning al-Himyari — from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the best prayer after the obligatory? He said: The depth of the night. And he was asked about the best fasting after the month of Ramadan? He said: The month of Allah which you call al-Muharram. And this hadith — thus Abu 'Awanah and Za'idah narrated it from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, and it is the correct one. And 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated it from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr did not preserve it; the hadith belongs to Za'idah and Abu 'Awanah."
"9519","Shihab ibn Mudlij al-Ka'bi. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us: Hafs ibn 'Umar narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: al-Qalus bint 'Ulaybah narrated to me — and she was under Shihab ibn Mudlij al-Ka'bi — that he was in Basra then became a Bedouin, settling at al-Lahabah, where his wealth and children multiplied. Then his sons exchanged insults among their people, saying: O sons of the hypocrite, your father abandoned emigration and became a Bedouin. And he felt it grievously in himself that he was insulted with that. So he called his son Salman, who brought him three riding camels; he mounted his servant on one baggage camel, and he and his son departed, going until they came to the Baqi' of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Madinah. Then he took the hand of his son Salman until they came to al-Dawsi Abu Hurayrah, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating to the people. The first thing they understood from him was that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Among the best of people are two men: a man who spends his wealth in the path of Allah Almighty, then strives with himself until he descends upon lands it grieves the enemy that he descends upon, then dies or is killed. Or a man of the desert folk among his camels, withdrawing from the evils of people, establishing the five prayers, giving the due of his wealth, and worshipping Allah until certainty — death — comes to him. So Shihab knelt upon his knees until he faced him, and said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, by the One in whose hand is Abu Hurayrah's soul — until he swore it to her three times. So Shihab deemed sufficient the verdict he had come seeking. Then he stood and prayed prostrations, then came to his mounts and rode them until they left Madinah behind their backs. Then he said to his son: By the One in whose hand is Shihab's soul, were it not for what al-Dawsi narrated to me, I would never have become a Bedouin for an hour except as a passing traveler. Then he returned, softened to his guest and his questioner, and remained fixed in his gathering place until he died."
"9520","Abu al-Malih. 'Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Humayd, from Abu al-Malih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deceit and trickery are in the Fire. And 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Humayd is not a preserver; only what he is alone with is written from his hadith; and we do not know of anyone who shared with him in this hadith besides him from Abu Hurayrah."
"9521","Muhammad ibn Hassan narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-'Aliyah or another, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a horse, and each of its strides reached as far as his sight; so he traveled, and Jibril (peace be upon him) traveled with him. He came upon a people who sow in a day and reap in a day; whenever they reaped it returned as it was. He said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are the strivers in the path of Allah; the good deed is multiplied for them seven hundredfold, and whatever they spend of anything, He replaces it. Then he came upon a people whose heads were crushed with rock; whenever they were crushed they returned as they were, without any pause from that for them. He said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are those whose heads were heavy away from prayer. Then he came upon a people with patches on their backs and patches on their fronts, driven as cattle are driven, to dari' and zaqqum and the embers of Hell. He said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are those who do not pay the charities of their wealth; and Allah did not wrong them, and Allah is not unjust to the servants. Then he came upon a people with meat in a pot, cooked, and other meat raw and foul; they began eating the foul and leaving the cooked good. He said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: This is the man of your ummah who rises from beside his lawful wife and goes to the foul woman, spending the night with her until morning; and the woman rises from beside her lawful good husband and goes to the foul man, spending the night with him until morning. Then he came upon a man who had gathered a great bundle he could not carry, yet wished to add to it. He said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is the man of your ummah upon whom are the trusts of people; he cannot fulfill them, yet he adds to them. Then he came upon a people whose lips and tongues were clipped with iron shears; whenever they were clipped they returned as they were, without pause from that for them. He said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: The preachers of tribulation. Then he came upon a small stone from which a great bull emerges; the bull tries to re-enter whence it came out but cannot. He said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is the man who speaks the grave word then regrets it, wishing to take it back but unable. Then he came upon a valley and found a pleasant scent, and found the scent of musk with a sound. He said: What is this? He said: The voice of Paradise saying: O Lord, bring me my people and what You promised me. Then he came upon a valley and heard a repugnant sound. He said: O Jibril, what is this sound? He said: This is the voice of Hell saying: O Lord, bring me my people and what You promised me. Then he traveled until he came to Bayt al-Maqdis and dismounted, tying his horse to a rock, and prayed with the angels. When the prayer ended, they said: O Jibril, who is this with you? He said: This is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, seal of the prophets. They said: And has he been sent for? He said: Yes. They said: Allah has greeted him as a brother and successor; what an excellent brother and excellent successor. Then they met the souls of the prophets, who praised their Lord: Ibrahim, Musa, Dawud, Sulayman, and 'Isa, each praising his Lord for His favors. And Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised his Lord, saying: Praise be to Allah who sent me as a mercy to the worlds, and to all mankind as a bringer of glad tidings and a warner; sent down upon me the Furqan, wherein is the clarification of all things; made my ummah the best ummah brought forth for mankind; made my ummah a middle nation; made my ummah the first and the last; expanded for me my breast, removed from me my burden, raised for me my mention, and made me an opener and a seal. Ibrahim (peace be upon him) said: For this, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has surpassed you. Then he was brought three covered vessels: water, milk, and wine; he drank of the milk until quenched and declined the wine. It was said to him: You are right; it shall be forbidden to your ummah. Then he was taken up through the seven heavens, meeting Adam, 'Isa and Yahya, Yusuf, Idris, Harun, Musa, and Ibrahim, peace be upon them; and saw the Lote-tree of the Utmost, from whose base emerge rivers of water, milk, wine, and purified honey. His Lord said to him: Ask. He mentioned the favors given to Ibrahim, Musa, Dawud, Sulayman, and 'Isa. His Lord said: I have taken you as a close friend; I sent you to all mankind, made your ummah the first and the last, made you the first of prophets in creation and the last in mission, gave you seven of the oft-repeated and the endings of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, and made you an opener and a seal. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Lord favored me with six: terror cast into my enemy's hearts over a month's journey; spoils made lawful for me; the earth made for me a mosque and a purifier; the openings and compendia of speech; my ummah displayed to me; and I was commanded with fifty prayers. He returned to Musa, who kept sending him back to his Lord to ask lightening for his ummah, until they were reduced to five. He said: I have returned to my Lord until I felt shy; I shall not return to Him. It was said to him: As you held yourself to five, it shall suffice you as fifty; every good deed is tenfold. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated except with this isnad through this chain."
"9522","Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muhajir, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Hurayrah, do you have anything with you? I said: Yes. So I brought out dates from a provision bag with me; there were twenty-seven dates in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed them, with people present, and said: Eat in the name of Allah. So they ate and some remained. He said: O Abu Hurayrah, return it to the bag; when you wish to take anything from it, put your hand in it and do not pour it out. He said: It remained with me until 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed."
"9523","And Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from a freedman of Abu Bakrah, meaning Muhajir, from Abu al-'Aliyah, he said: Abu Hurayrah said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Hurayrah, do you have anything with you? He said: I said: Yes. He said: So I brought out dates from a provision bag with me; there were twenty-seven dates in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed them beside him, then mentioned something like the hadith of Hammad ibn Zayd. He said: It remained with me, eating from it, until the siege of 'Uthman, when it fell from me while I was occupied away from it. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Hatim, nor do we know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah with this wording through a better isnad than this isnad."
"9524","Bishr ibn Adam ibn bint Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abu Khaldah narrated to us, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Of whom are you? I said: Of Daws. He said: I did not think there was anyone in Daws with good in him. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayrah, nor do we know for it a path from Abu Hurayrah except this path."
"9525","Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi. 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath and 'Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit — meaning al-Bunani — from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, that Abu Hurayrah was on a journey; when they alighted, tables were laid and they sent for him while he was praying. He said: I am fasting. When they were about to finish, he came and ate. The people looked at their messenger, who said: What are you looking at? By Allah, he informed me that he is fasting. Abu Hurayrah said: He spoke the truth; by Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts the month of patience and three days of every month has fasted the whole of time. I have fasted three days of every month; so I am one who breaks fast by Allah's alleviation and fasts by Allah's multiplication. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Abu Hurayrah except Abu 'Uthman, nor do we preserve it except from the hadith of Hammad, from Thabit, from Abu 'Uthman."
"9526","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Zayd ibn Akhzam said: 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: the witr before sleep, the two rak'ahs of Duha, and fasting three days of every month. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Abu al-Tayyah except 'Abd al-Warith; nor did Abu al-Tayyah narrate in musnad form from Abu 'Uthman other than this hadith."
"9527","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us with it: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Shimr al-Duba'i narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu 'Uthman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Abu Shimr, from Abu 'Uthman, except Shu'bah. This wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through many paths."
"9528","Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: It reached me that Abu Hurayrah narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah, blessed and exalted be He, multiplies the good deed for His believing servant a millionfold. So I set out and met Abu Hurayrah, and said: It reached me from you that you say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah multiplies the good deed a millionfold? He said: Yes; I heard him say: For the good deed two million good deeds. Then he recited this verse: Allah does not wrong even the weight of an atom, up to His saying: a great reward. Who knows the measure of what Allah called great? And this hadith — we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah with this isnad."
"9529","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Maymun narrated to us, Abu 'Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to announce that there is no prayer except with the recitation of the Opening of the Book, and what is added. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah; and Ja'far ibn Maymun is Basran, well known."
"9530","Al-Walid ibn 'Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I am the first to open the gate of Paradise; then a woman calls to me, and I say to her: Who are you? She says: I am a woman who sat devoted to my orphans. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this isnad. And 'Abd al-Salam ibn 'Ajlan is a man of Basra, well known."
"9531","Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw therein a servant who had done no good except that he used to remove harm from the path of Muslims; so Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise thereby. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain, nor do we know of these two hadiths narrated from 'Abd al-Salam except by Ya'qub ibn Ishaq, and he is trustworthy, well known."
"9532","'Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from al-Jurayri — and he is Sa'id ibn Iyas — from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When your rulers are the best of you, your rich the generous among you, and your affairs counsel among you, then the back of the earth is better for you than its belly; and when your rulers are the worst of you, your rich the miserly among you, and your affairs to your women, then the belly of the earth is better for you than its back. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah, nor do we know for it a path other than this path."
"9533","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Asim narrated to us, Salih al-Murri — and he is Salih ibn Bashir — narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over Hamzah ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib when he was martyred and looked at a sight more painful to the heart than any he had seen; he looked at him mutilated and said: May Allah's mercy be upon you; as far as I knew you were indeed joining of kin and a doer of good deeds. By Allah, were it not for the grief of those after you over you, it would please me to leave you until Allah gathers you from the bellies of beasts. Yet by Allah, for that I shall indeed mutilate seventy like your mutilation. So Jibril (peace be upon him) descended upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting: And if you punish, punish with the like of what you were punished with, to the end of the verse. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expiated and refrained from that. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah except through this chain."
"9534","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed dates among us; I received five dates, or four dates and a dry one; and I saw the dry one the hardest of them for my molar. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu 'Uthman from Abu Hurayrah."
"9535","'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq. Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-'Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9536","And Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated it to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and the wording is Hushaym's — he said: The best of my ummah are the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then there shall arise a people who love fatness and make vows but do not fulfill them. Something like this wording has been narrated through other chains, but we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah with this isnad."
"9537","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the soul of the believer departs, two angels receive it and ascend with it, mentioning its pleasant scent and musk. The people of heaven say: A good soul has come from the direction of earth; may Allah bless you and the body you used to inhabit. So he is taken to his Lord, blessed and exalted be He. It is said: Take him to the end of the two terms. And he mentioned the disbeliever, mentioning his stench; he is taken up, and the people of heaven say: A foul soul has come from the direction of earth, mentioning cursing. So they proceed with him to his Lord, and it is said: Take him to the end of the two terms. Abu Hurayrah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the stench, he put his hand or his garment over his nose. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it with this wording except Abu Hurayrah, nor from him except 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, nor did anyone narrate it except Hammad from Budayl."
"9538","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever strikes with a lash unjustly shall be retaliated upon on the Day of Resurrection. And this wording — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah. 'Imran was differed upon: Ibn Raja' said: From 'Imran, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah. And Muhammad ibn Bilal said: From 'Imran, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah. And Ibn Raja' is more famous than Muhammad ibn Bilal."
"9539","Abu Hatim al-Sijistani narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9540","And Ibrahim ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated it to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It would not please me that Uhud were gold for me, spending it in the path of Allah, dying the day I die with a dinar of it still with me. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other than this chain; this isnad is a sound isnad."
"9541","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Budayl, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave and from the punishment of Hell and the Dajjal. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Budayl except Shu'bah."
"9542","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed us: Khalid narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes up, let him not dip his hand into his vessel until he has washed it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq except Khalid, and it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through many paths."
"9543","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us, from Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as though he were your companion, and I saw Musa (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tall and dark, and I saw 'Isa (peace be upon him) red and curly-haired. And this hadith has been narrated by others besides 'Ali from Khalid."
"9544","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: Ibn 'Abbas addressed us one day after 'Asr until the sun set and the stars appeared, and the people kept calling out to him: The prayer, the prayer; and among the people was a man from Banu Tamim. Ibn 'Abbas said: Do you teach me the Sunnah? May you have no mother. I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combine Zuhr and 'Asr and Maghrib and 'Isha. He said: So I met Abu Hurayrah and he agreed with him. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from the hadith of 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn 'Abbas and Abu Hurayrah, except from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq; nor do we know of al-Zubayr narrating 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq in musnad form from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"9545","Qasamah ibn Zuhayr. Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the believer is attended, angels come to him with silk containing musk and bundles of basil; his soul is drawn out as a hair is drawn from dough. It is said: O tranquil soul, come out content and pleasing to the spirit of Allah and His honor. When his soul exits, it is placed upon that musk and basil, the silk is folded over it, and he is taken to 'Illiyyin. And when the disbeliever is attended, angels come to him with a coarse cloth containing an ember; his soul is wrenched out with severe wrenching. It is said: O foul soul, come out wrathful and wrathfully dealt with, to Allah's humiliation and punishment. When his soul exits, it is placed upon that ember, the cloth is folded over it, and he is taken to Sijjin."
"9546","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Qasamah ibn Zuhayr al-Mazini, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the believer is attended, the angels of mercy come to him with white silk, saying: Come out content and pleasing to the spirit of Allah and basil and a Lord not angry. So he comes out like the pleasantest scent of musk, until some hand him to others to smell him, until they bring him to the gate of heaven. They say: How pleasant is this scent that has come to you from earth. Whenever they come to a heaven they say to them the like of that, until they bring him to the souls of the believers; they are more joyful with him than one of you with his absent one when he arrives. They say: What did so-and-so do? They say: Leave him to rest, for he was in the grief of the world. When he recovers or rests, he says to them: Has he not come to you? For he has died! They say: He has gone to his mother Hawiyah. As for the disbeliever, the angels of punishment come to him with a coarse cloth, saying: Come out wrathful, wrathfully dealt with, to Allah's punishment and wrath. So he comes out like the foulest stench of a carcass; they proceed with him to the gate of the earth. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith with this wording except Qatadah, from Qasamah, from Abu Hurayrah. Qasamah is a man of Basra; Qatadah, 'Imran ibn Hudayr, Sulayman al-Taymi, and al-Jurayri narrated from him."
"9547","Zurarah from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"9548","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9549","And Nasr ibn 'Ali and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us — 'Amr said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, and Nasr said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Mis'ar informed us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted be He, has overlooked for my ummah what their souls speak of, so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it. And this hadith was narrated by Shu'bah, Sa'id, Mis'ar, Hisham, Hammad, and Abu 'Awanah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We do not know it narrated from the Prophet through a sound chain except from Abu Hurayrah. The preserved hadith is only from Zurarah from Abu Hurayrah."
"9550","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a woman spends the night abandoning her husband's bed, the angels curse her until he is pleased with her — or he said — until she returns. And this wording has been narrated with similar but not its wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other chains, and from Abu Hurayrah from the hadith of Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah; it has been narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam and from Ibn Abi Awfa."
"9551","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah al-Basri — and his name is Mujja'ah — narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with food, and he said: Place it on the ground. Or he said: On the earth. And this wording was narrated by al-Hasan in mursal form, and narrated from Ibn 'Umar; I think in it is: I am only a servant; I eat as the servant eats."
"9552","Abu Maymunah from Abu Hurayrah. And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when I see you my eye is delighted and my soul is pleased; and when I do not see you my soul is not pleased. Or a word similar to it."
"9553","Abu Hassan from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu al-Salil, from Abu Hassan, he said: I said to Abu Hurayrah: I have two sons; will you narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith that comforts our souls concerning our dead? He said: Yes. Their young are the little ones of Paradise; one of them meets his father, taking hold of his garment — or he said: his hand — as I take hold of the edge of this garment of yours; he does not desist or stop until he admits him to Paradise. And this wording — we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayrah, nor do we know for it a path from Abu Hurayrah except this path."
"9554","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qati'i narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, and from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man visited a brother of his for Allah while he was in another village; so Allah, blessed and exalted be He, stationed an angel upon his path, who said: Where do you intend? He said: A brother of mine in this village, visiting him. He said: Is there any favor of his upon you that you foster? He said: No; I loved him for Allah. He said: I am the messenger of Allah, blessed and exalted be He, to you; He has loved you as you loved him for Him. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from 'Asim, from Abu Hassan, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah; nor from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad; nor is this wording narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"9555","Bashir ibn Nuhayk. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Locusts of gold rained upon Ayyub, and he began picking them up. He said: O Ayyub, did I not enrich you? He said: O Lord, who is ever sated of Your mercy? And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from another chain with other than this wording; and narrated from Anas likewise with other than this wording."
"9556","And Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two wives and inclines to one of them over the other shall come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides fallen. And this wording — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah, nor do we know for it a path from Abu Hurayrah except through this path."
"9557","Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs narrated to us, 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes strike my shoulder and say: Love Banu Tamim. And this wording — we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"9558","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks into a people's house without their permission and they put out his eye, there is no blood money for him nor retaliation. And this hadith has been narrated with similar wording from Abu Hurayrah through other chains; and it has been narrated from others besides Abu Hurayrah concerning dislike of looking into a people's house through other chains."
"9559","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nuhayk, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays one rak'ah of the dawn prayer then the sun rises, let him pray another to it. And this wording — we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah from him."
"9560","Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali said: Abu Dawud narrated to us: 'Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Nothing is more noble to Allah than supplication. And this wording — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah, nor do we know for it a path except this path."
"9561","And with his isnad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said. And Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three men among those before you went out seeking provision for their families; rain befell them, so they took refuge in a mountain or a cave, and a rock fell upon them — meaning it fell upon the mouth of the cave. One of them said to another: The rock has fallen, the trace is effaced, and none knows your place but Allah; so supplicate to Allah with your most firmly established deeds. One of them said: O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I would milk for them in their vessel; when I came to them while they slept, I would stand waiting until they woke, whenever they woke; I disliked that their drowsiness turn in their heads, and when they woke they drank. O Allah, if You know that I only did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So a third of the rock moved. The other said: O Allah, if You know that there was a woman who pleased me, and I sought her but she refused to yield herself to me until I offered her a payment; when she took her payment and her soul settled, I left her. O Allah, if You know that I only did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So a third of the rock moved. The other said: O Allah, if You know that I hired a laborer to work for me a day; he worked, then came seeking his wage; I gave it to him but he did not take it, disdaining it. So I multiplied it for him until it became of all wealth; then he came seeking his wage, and I said: Take all this; had I wished I would not have given him except his wage. O Allah, if You know that I only did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So the rock moved, and they went out walking. And this wording and the like and near to it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through many chains. It was narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Ibn 'Umar through many chains, and from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, and 'Aishah."
"9562","Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah 'Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed women among men who imitate women, and men among women who imitate men. And this hadith — we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, except Sa'id ibn Bashir; we only preserve it from the hadith of Abu al-Mughirah, from Sa'id. It has been narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who resembles men or wears men's clothing, and cursed the masculine woman, and cursed the effeminate among men and the masculine among women."
"9563","Al-Hasan. Al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us, Ibn 'Ulayyah — meaning Isma'il — narrated to us, from Yunus — meaning Ibn 'Ubayd — from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will preserve from what Allah obligated upon him a word, two words, or three, acting upon them and teaching them? I said: I. So I spread my cloak, and he narrated to me until the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ended; then I gathered it to me. I hope I shall not forget anything I heard. It has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah with similar wording but not this wording through other chains."
"9564","Muhammad ibn 'Ammar al-Razi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We were seated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a cloud passed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what this is? We said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: This is the cloud, and it is driven to a people of a land who do not worship Him. Do you know what is above that? They said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: A restrained wave and a guarded roof. Do you know what is above that? They said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: Above that is a heaven. Do you know what is above that? They said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: Above that is a heaven. Do you know what is between them? They said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: Between them is a journey of five hundred years — until he counted seven heavens, between every heaven a journey of five hundred years. Then he said: Do you know what is above that? They said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: Above that is the Throne. And he said: Do you know what this is? They said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: This is the earth. He said: Do you know what is beneath it? They said: Allah and His messenger know best. He said: Between them is a journey of five hundred years. Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul: Had one of you acted down to seven earths, to the lowest, he would reach Allah. Then he recited: He is the First and the Last and the Manifest and the Hidden, the verse. And this wording — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad, nor do we know of this wording narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by Abu Hurayrah."
"9565","Al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Malik, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Race to deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the private affair of one of you, the general affair, and the beast of the earth. And this wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through another chain; I do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayrah."
"9566","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Hisham al-Mughirah ibn Salamah narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women who seek divorce without cause are the hypocrites. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain; it has been narrated from Thawban from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9567","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn Abi Khayrah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9568","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: 'Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Khayrah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A time shall come upon people in which people consume usury; whoever of them does not consume it, its dust reaches him. And this wording — we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him) except from Abu Hurayrah with this isnad."
"9569","Ziyad ibn Rabah. Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ziyad ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever leaves obedience and parts from the community and dies upon that, his death is a death of ignorance; and whoever goes out against my ummah striking its righteous and its wicked, showing no restraint from its believer nor fulfilling the covenant of its covenanted one, he is not of me; and whoever is killed under the banner of zealotry, angered for partisanship, his killing is a killing of ignorance. And this wording — we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9570","And Yunus ibn 'Ubayd narrated it from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, he said: From Ziyad ibn Matar, from Abu Hurayrah. Thus 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us. He said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan — meaning al-Thawri — narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ziyad ibn Matar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the correct one is the hadith of Hammad ibn Zayd."
"9571","Yahya ibn Ya'mar: Abdah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who entices a woman against her husband, or a slave against his master. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad, and it has been narrated from Buraydah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this isnad is better than the isnad of Buraydah."
"9572","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ismail ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Hakim, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9573","And I heard Abdullah, the son-in-law of Shayban ibn Farrukh, saying: Abdulmalik al-Juddi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and the wording is the wording of Yahya ibn Ya'mar - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant will be held accountable for is the prayer; if it was complete, otherwise it will be said: Does he have any voluntary prayers? Then the obligatory will be completed from his voluntary prayers. And this hadith was narrated by Hammad ibn Salamah, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know anyone who said: from Abu Hurayrah, except Abdulmalik al-Juddi."
"9574","And I found in my book, from Muhammad ibn Marzuq, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Aban - meaning Ibn Yazid - from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Hakim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant will be held accountable for is his prayer; if it was sound then he has succeeded and prospered, and if it was bad then he has failed and lost. And we do not know this report narrated except from Abu Hurayrah and Tamim al-Dari, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"9575","Shutayr ibn Nahar, and they said: Sumayr: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Having a good opinion of Allah is part of the good worship of Allah."
"9576","And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Sumayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Had My servants obeyed Me, I would have given them rain by night, and let the sun rise upon them by day, and would not have let them hear the sound of thunder. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Having a good opinion of Allah is part of the good worship of Allah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Renew your faith. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we renew our faith? He said: Renew your faith by saying: There is no god but Allah. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle, from Abu Hurayrah, with this isnad."
"9577","Abdurrahman ibn Adam: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abdurrahman ibn Adam, and he is the freedman of Umm Burthun, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, blessed and exalted, prescribed Friday for those who were before us, but they differed over it, so Allah guided us to it; thus people are followers of us: the Jews on Saturday and the Christians on Sunday."
"9578","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abdurrahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and Abu Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, similar to it, and it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from several angles, and narrated from Hudhayfah and others from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9579","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdurrahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9580","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abdurrahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9581","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abdurrahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9582","And Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdurrahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Prophets are brothers from co-wives; their mothers are different but their religion is one, and I am the closest of people to Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon him); there was no prophet between me and him, and he will come, so when you see him, recognize him: a man of medium stature, between reddish and white, as if his head is dripping though no wetness has touched it, between two garments dyed with saffron; he will break the cross, kill the pig, make wealth abundant, abolish the jizyah, and destroy all creeds except Islam, and Allah, blessed and exalted, will destroy the false messiah, the Dajjal, and security will be placed upon the earth until the lion grazes with camels, the wolf with sheep, and children play with snakes without harming them; he will remain forty years, then die, and the Muslims will pray over him. And this hadith was narrated by Said and Hisham and Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj and Hammam, all of them narrated it from Qatadah, from Abdurrahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, and some of these words have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles, namely: The Prophets are brothers from co-wives. As for: Security will be placed upon the earth, it was narrated by Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, and it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from another angle."
"9583","Abu Umar al-Ghudani: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu Umar al-Ghudani, who said: I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah when a man from Banu Amir ibn Sasaah passed, and they said: This is the wealthiest Amiri. He said: Bring him back to me. So they brought him back to him, and he said to him: I have been told that you are a man of great wealth? He said: By Allah, I have a hundred red camels and a hundred dark camels, until he listed kinds of camels, valuable slaves, and tethered horses. Abu Hurayrah said: Beware of the camels' hooves and the sheep's cloven hooves, and he repeated that until the Amiri's color began to change. He said: What is that, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever has camels and does not pay their due in their hardship and their ease - we said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their hardship and their ease? He said: In their difficult times and their easy times - they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their best and fattest state, and a wide flat plain will be spread for them, and they will trample him with their hooves; every time the last of them passes him, the first of them will be brought back upon him, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among people and he sees his path. And if he has cattle and does not give their due in their hardship and their ease, they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their best and fattest state, and a wide flat plain will be spread for them, and every cloven-hoofed one will trample him with its hoof, and every horned one will butt him with its horn; every time the last of them passes him, the first of them will be brought back upon him, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among people and he sees his path. And if he has sheep and does not give their due in their hardship and their ease, they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their best and fattest state, and a wide flat plain will be spread for them, and every horned one will butt him with its horn, every time the last of them passes him, the first of them will be brought back upon him, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among people and he sees his path. They said: O Abu Hurayrah, what is the due of camels? He said: To give the precious one, lend the rich-milked one, lend the stallion for covering, and give milk to drink."
"9584","And Talq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Umar al-Ghudani, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know that Abu Umar al-Ghudani narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith, and we do not know anyone narrated from him except Qatadah, and it was narrated by more than one from Qatadah, so we sufficed with those we heard, and it was narrated from Abu Hurayrah in the hadith of Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah, and from Asim from Abu Hurayrah, similar to parts of it, and narrated in the hadith of Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to that."
"9585","Abdullah ibn Rabah: Muhammad ibn Muthanna and Ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hasten to do deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its setting place, the Dajjal, the smoke, the Beast of the earth, the private affair of one of you, and the general affair. And it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from another angle, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatadah from Abdullah ibn Rabah except Imran al-Qattan."
"9586","Abu Ayyub al-Azdi: Muhammad narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face. And similar words to this have been narrated with other than this wording, from Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn Umar, and Abu Said."
"9587","Bushayr ibn Kab: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bushayr ibn Kab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you dispute about the road, make it seven cubits. And this hadith has been narrated with similar words from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, and from Abu Qilabah from Anas."
"9588","Aws ibn Khalid: Amr ibn Ali and Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered in three thirds: a third riding mounts, a third on their feet, and a third on their faces. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from this angle, from Abu Hurayrah, with this isnad."
"9589","Abdulwarith ibn Abdissamad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of one who hears wisdom but acts only on the worst of it is the likeness of a man who came to a shepherd and said: Give me a sheep from your flock in portions. He said: Go and take a sheep by its best ear. So he went and took hold of the ear of the flock's dog. And we do not know anyone narrated these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayrah."
"9590","And I found in my book, from Talut ibn Abbad, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Beast will come out with the seal of Sulayman and the staff of Musa; it will brighten the faces of the believers with the staff, and seal the nose of the disbeliever with the seal, until the people gathered at the watering place will say: O believer, this one, and: O disbeliever, that one. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"9591","Al-Tufawi: Muammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim, and he is Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from al-Tufawi, who said: I came to Madinah and stayed with Abu Hurayrah for a month, and he narrated to me that he fell ill, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and said: Where is the young Dawsi? It was said: There he is, in a corner of the mosque, ill. So he came and placed his hand on me and spoke kind words, then said: If Satan makes me forget something of my prayer, let the men say Subhan Allah and the women clap. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in his prayer with two rows of men behind him and a row of women, or two rows of women and a row of men, and he prayed and forgot nothing. When he finished his prayer, he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Now then, is it not that a man may close a door and lower a curtain and conceal himself with Allah's concealment, then go out and say: I did such and such with my wife? A young maiden stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, they do that, and they (women) do that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you the likeness of that? They said: What is its likeness? He said: The likeness of a male devil meeting a female devil in a lane, then having intercourse with her while people watch. Then he said: Let no woman touch another woman intimately, nor a man another man, except the child and the parent. Then he said: The perfume of men is scent without color, and the perfume of women is color without scent. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah in its entirety except with this isnad, though parts of it have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah and from others."
"9592","Muhammad ibn Ziyad: Muhammad ibn Abdilmalik al-Qurashi and Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us; Ahmad said: Hammad informed us, and Muhammad ibn Abdilmalik said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey? And this hadith was narrated from Muhammad ibn Ziyad by Yunus ibn Ubayd and Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj and Hammad ibn Salamah and Abbad ibn Mansur and Umar ibn Abi Khalifah and Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, so we sufficed with Hammad ibn Zayd."
"9593","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Our Lord, blessed and exalted, wonders at people who are led to Paradise in chains. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other than this angle, and this isnad is among the best isnads narrated from Abu Hurayrah on that, and it has been narrated from Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9594","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abdirrahman informed us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad said: From Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves against the Fire even with half a date. And these words have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other than this angle, and this isnad from Abu Hurayrah is the best and most authentic narrated on that. And it has been narrated from Aishah: Ibn Abi Mulaykah and Abul Aliyah narrated it from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her. And narrated from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, from several angles: Muhill ibn Khalifah and Abbad ibn Hubaysh and Khaythamah ibn Abdirrahman and Abdullah ibn Maqil and others narrated it from Adi. And narrated from Humayd from Anas, and from Abu Raja from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and narrated from Jarir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"9595","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, ar-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this isnad, and it was narrated from Abu Said al-Khudri, and from Usamah ibn Zayd, and from an-Numan ibn Bashir, and from Abul Malih from his father, and it has been narrated from Umar ibn al-Khattab from more than one angle that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But so-and-so did not give thanks."
"9596","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, ar-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Hajj: Is it every year? I think he said: Had I said yes, it would have become obligatory, and had it become obligatory, only a few would have acted upon it. And these words have been narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib, and from Anas ibn Malik and Ibn Abbas, and others, and the most authentic isnad narrated on that is the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah."
"9597","Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, ar-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dates from charity dates, and when they were placed, al-Hasan took a date from them and his saliva flowed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kikh! Do you not know that the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do not eat charity? And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah, and ar-Rabi added a word in it, namely: Kikh. And there have been narrated on the dislike of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating charity, hadiths: narrated from Ibn Abbas, and from Abu Rafi, and Anas ibn Malik, and Abdullah ibn Amr, and Aishah, and from Abdirrahman ibn Abi Layla from his father."
"9598","Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, ar-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said to the soul: Come out. It said: I will not come out except unwillingly. He said: Come out even if unwilling. And we do not know this hadith narrated except by Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor narrated it from Abu Hurayrah except Muhammad ibn Ziyad, nor from Muhammad except ar-Rabi ibn Muslim, and ar-Rabi ibn Muslim is trustworthy and reliable."
"9599","Ammar ibn Abi Ammar: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Zayd and Yunus ibn Ubayd narrating from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: As for Ali ibn Zayd, he raised it, and as for Yunus, he did not go beyond Abu Hurayrah, on this verse: By the witnessing and the witnessed: he said: The day of Arafah and the day of Friday, and: By the promised day: the Day of Resurrection."
"9600","Ibrahim ibn Nasr ar-Razi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I never witnessed any booty with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except he allotted me a share of it, except the day of Khaybar, for it was specially for the people of Hudaybiyah; Abu Hurayrah and Abu Musa had come between Hudaybiyah and Khaybar. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except Ammar ibn Abi Ammar."
